  (395182695672::bigint, 404187085048::bigint, null::bigint, 326468273357::bigint, '11/12 CALL NOTES

Overview
Intangia presented their AI-powered biotech platform to GT Life Science team, showcasing their ability to identify promising drug combinations through statistical analysis of patents, papers, and clinical trials. The platform uses fine-tuned BERT models to extract keywords and track co-occurrence patterns, achieving 67% accuracy versus 50-55% industry standard. Intangia currently has 5-10 paying customers with pilot deals under $10k for 3-month periods, expecting their first yearly license in January-February. They''re exploring partnerships with Phase 5 for biological validation and potential Snowflake integration for enterprise deployment. GT Life Science identified potential collaboration opportunities and suggested key industry contacts including David Pardo at Evotech, Malcolm Horsley at Avant Garde, and connections through Chemify. The discussion revealed plans for Q1 KPI measurement with pilots, Q2 transition to revenue-generating business, and potential fundraising based on demonstrated ROI metrics.


Action Items
John Harris:
Will discuss organizing an AI and life science showcase event with Tom Halliday to help Intangia demonstrate their platform
Will facilitate introductions to David Pardo at Evotech, Malcolm Horsley at Avant Garde, and Richard Cox at Chemify if Intangia finds them relevant after review
Olivier Collart:
Will meet with Chemify founder through Inside Ventures introduction at J.P. Morgan event
Will review Mindsoft.com website to assess potential data partnership opportunities before requesting introduction
Topics
Team Introductions and Company Background (0:25)
John Harris introduced GT Life Science team including himself as CTO and co-founder with previous roles as chief architect at GlaxoSmithKline and global CTO at Mundy Pharma. Team includes Nikita as CEO based in UK, Vikra in sales ops, and Merxhan heading AI engineering who won NASA award for wildfire management AI in North Macedonia. Olivier Collart founded Intangia two years ago with background in correlating IP data with performance metrics, incubated by biotech VC. Core team of four full-time remote workers includes Greg on frontend/UX in London, Tom as head of product in Lyon France, and Sam as backend engineer in Slovakia.


Product Overview and Core Functionality (8:28)
Intangia serves VCs, hedge funds, early-stage biotechs, and mid-cap pharma like Serepta. Platform extracts meaningful keywords from papers, patents, and clinical trials using machine learning pipeline while maintaining metadata including authors, organizations, PICOS from clinical trials, and investor information. System maps data onto ontologies and tracks activity across concepts over time. Example shown with PD1 cancer target demonstrating papers, patents, clinical trials over time plus assets created and company exposure. Tool identifies co-occurring keywords and uses statistical modeling to determine meaningful relationships, successfully identifying 70% of keywords showing translation pattern from papers to patents to clinic.


Partnership Strategy and Market Expansion (15:07)
Developing partnership with Phase 5 for biological causal relationship validation to reduce noise in combination predictions. Inside Ventures investor connecting Intangia with Chemify for potential three-way collaboration combining discovery insights, biological validation, and synthesis capabilities. Platform addresses market demand for bispecific and trispecific combinations, automatically identifying potential ADC with PD1 combinations. Strategy includes expansion from R&amp;D to BD and IP teams within pharma companies for cross-selling opportunities.


Building Snowflake accelerator integration allowing direct plugin to client environments without data leaving premises. System can process files from S3 buckets and overlay proprietary data with Intangia''s dataset. Use cases range from lab notebook integration to BD deck analysis for competitive intelligence. Vision includes becoming application layer connecting multiple data providers with enrichment capabilities. Technical integration depends on proving use case value and measuring KPIs before addressing complex pharma data infrastructure challenges.


Current Business Model and Monetization (34:26)
Company has 5-10 paying customers with pilot deals typically under $10k for 3-month periods. Expects first yearly license starting January-February with Geneva customer showing strong interest after recent meeting. Currently pilot-generating rather than revenue-generating business, targeting transition to sustainable revenue model in Q2. Plans to focus on limited number of R&amp;D heads to demonstrate use case, measure KPIs, and prove execution before scaling. Pricing strategy varies by company size with smaller biotechs paying for competitive intelligence automation, larger companies charged per project with potential token usage fees.


Technical Architecture and Implementation (42:45)
Backend uses fine-tuned BERT model trained on patents by Google, specifically optimized for biotech and pharma keywords with 67% accuracy versus 50-55% industry standard. System processes papers, patents, clinical trials weekly through AWS ECS cluster with Aurora database. Pipeline incorporates ontologies like SNOMED and DOID for keyword categorization and hierarchical organization. Uses OpenSearch for occurrence tracking with plans to optimize scalability issues. Implements embeddings for keyword clustering, organization similarity analysis, and graph visualizations showing company portfolios and therapeutic area positioning.


Industry Connections and Growth Opportunities (59:07)
GT Life Science suggested key industry contacts including David Pardo at Evotech who previously described molecular research challenges matching Intangia''s solution, Malcolm Horsley at Avant Garde for operational insights, and Mindsoft.com for potential data partnerships. Discussion of organizing AI and life science showcase event with GT as foundation partner to demonstrate platform capabilities to broader audience. Connections could accelerate pilot conversion to licenses and provide roadmap guidance through industry feedback.', 'VS', '2025-12-19 04:21'),
