  (333098367173::bigint, 352726158559::bigint, null::bigint, 278186195187::bigint, '30/10 CALL NOTES (John, Nikita, Vika, Andrew M., Paulina and Paul Plater)


💼 Company OverviewInvestment: ~£20M total; initial investor (since 2016) spent £10M; current main backer is Highland and Universal Investments Ltd (Dame Ann Gloag).
Background: Originally expected to need £300k to reach market but heavily overspent; investors are patient but now demand a clear plan and ROI.
Status: Transitioning from internal restructuring to engaging external partners and seeking strategic direction.
🧠 Technical &amp; Product ChallengesTeam: High turnover, weak continuity, previously misaligned technical efforts (too experimental, little commercial focus).
Leadership: Current CTO is technically strong but lacks strategic leadership experience.
Development: Historically reactive, focusing on fixing problems rather than driving innovation or market needs.
⚙️ Hardware &amp; SoftwareOriginal devices: bed and wearable sensors.
Bed sensor replaced with Withings (3rd party).
Wearable was non-compliant and uncomfortable → replaced by SureSafe (includes fall detection).
Hardware was over-specified and costly; software/firmware lacked structure.
Focus now on stability, reliability, and 3rd-party integration.
👥 User ExperienceWearables are problematic for elderly/dementia users (comfort, usability, forgetfulness).
Explored radar, Wi-Fi sensing, audio-based monitoring — still immature or expensive.
Feedback calls for motion sensors, daily reporting, and platform integrations (UMO, councils, NHS).
🚀 Roadmap &amp; StrategyCurrent roadmap is tactical, not strategic — driven by issues, not vision.
GT proposed a two-phase approach:
Outside-in market research → identify competitors, differentiation, and user needs.
Strategic roadmap + governance setup → define priorities, align engineering with business, and enforce disciplined roadmap management.
Governance model inspired by Apple’s product planning — no ad hoc changes, structured remix/review process.
🌍 Market &amp; PositioningMarket has no dominant player; competitors differentiate by feature (fall detection, motion sensing).
Goal: build best-of-breed integrated solution combining 3rd-party tech into a seamless care ecosystem.
Focus on user experience, data insights, and commercial scalability.
💰 Funding &amp; InvestorsInvestors are cautious but supportive — seek evidence of focus and ROI.
CEO acknowledged spending £200k/month and wants to ensure better value from engineering investments.
✅ Next Steps / OutcomesGT to send modular proposal early next week:
Phase 1: Market research (small paid engagement).
Phase 2: Strategic roadmap &amp; governance setup.
Later: Potential engineering partnership to optimize internal spend and productivity.
CEO supportive, plans to present proposal to investors.
Possible in-person follow-up in London with Paulina &amp; Andrew.', 'VS', '2025-10-30 09:01'),
