Also temp-to-perm; long-term need.
Budget roughly US $75 k fully-loaded if in-house.
Project Manager (optional, fractional)
10 h/week for ~4 months to shepherd the website launch and coordinate stakeholders.
Budget placeholder about US $9 k total; client is undecided but wants costs.
5. Location and time-zone expectationsOpen to Eastern-European talent (Ukraine, Poland, Romania, Bulgaria, etc.) provided there is around five hours of daily overlap with US Eastern Time.
Near-shore options such as Canada or Mexico are also acceptable. Full overnight shifts are a non-starter.
6. Recruitment process and agreed next stepsJob descriptions:
• Client will refresh the full-stack JD.
• GT will draft the QA JD.
• Both exchanged by end of tomorrow (21 May 2025).
Pricing &amp; proposal: GT to send indicative costs with the JDs.
Kick-off call: pencilled for Thursday 22 May (09:00 ET preferred; 13:00 ET as fallback) with Casey present to finalise requirements and interview flow.
Candidate pipeline: first screened profile within 3–7 days of kick-off; three or four more candidates quickly after.
Interview-to-offer: typical duration about four weeks, but could close in one to two weeks if an early candidate is accepted.
Paperwork: MSA, NDA or LOI will run in parallel and not block recruiting.
7. Take-aways for GTEmphasise temp-to-perm flexibility and the ability to keep talent on GT’s payroll indefinitely if that proves easier for the client.
Candidates must be comfortable with ambiguous, fast-moving work and a “wear-all-hats” culture.
Time-zone overlap is critical; highlight engineers used to late-start schedules that provide five-hour ET crossover.
Speed matters, but cultural and technical alignment—especially Casey’s buy-in—are non-negotiable.', 'VS', '2025-05-15 11:36'),
