  (181846922475::bigint, 16199822573::bigint, null::bigint, 13348058097::bigint, '15/04 CALL NOTES (John, Andy, Vika, Umar)

The team recently launched Clinitouch 3, a rebuilt and improved version of their product, which went live in early March. The main focus now is to deprecate Clinitouch 2, which was previously targeted at the UK market, and to prepare for upcoming tenders in the region.
🛠️ Product and Tender DetailsTwo large UK tenders have been submitted. Results are expected by end of May.
If awarded, the team will need to scale significantly to meet a September/October go-live timeline.
Tender requirements include new technical asks, but Clinitouch 3 already meets many of them.
Current team:
3 developers + CTO (who also covers infrastructure).
Tech stack includes: Android, iOS apps, React frontend, backend services.
The QA team is small and junior, focused on manual testing. They need senior QA expertise, particularly for test automation and CI/CD support.
Device strategy now focuses on standard Bluetooth medical devices, integrated via HealthKit and Google Health Connect, instead of custom device integration.
🤝 GT Engagement ModelsGT introduced three service models:
Recruitment-as-a-Service – traditional external hiring.
Extended Team – dedicated developers sourced from Eastern Europe (Ukraine, Poland, Romania, Turkey), with flexible contracts, no recruitment fees, and easy conversion to in-house staff.
Project Teams – day-rate access to specialists like QA, DevOps, or UI/UX, used to augment short-term capacity.
Key advantages from GT:
Talent pool across multiple countries.
Strict screening process (only 1 of 8 candidates is passed on).
Team setup possible in ~4 weeks, if hiring managers provide fast feedback.
Optional Solution Architect support to evaluate current architecture and align it with tender specs.
Optional Delivery Managers and Happiness Managers to support onboarding, integration, and retention.
✅ Next StepsUmar (client) will:
Share current solution architecture for review.
Prepare job specs for QA/dev roles (placeholders or proxies are fine).
Outline tender scope and expected team size/complexity.
GT will:
Send a proposal covering both Extended Team and Project Team pricing.
If approved, send over an MSA (Master Service Agreement) for legal review (typically 1 week turnaround).
Begin sourcing immediately after green light.
💬 Other Discussion PointsClinitouch 2 is still live for a single UK customer, expected to sunset after the contract ends.
Umar and team have prior experience working with Eastern European outsourced teams.
GT emphasized the importance of rapid hiring cycles to avoid losing top talent during summer breaks.
Preference is to integrate GT hires directly into the core UK team, not as a separate unit.
GT can offer project management support if both tenders succeed and rapid scaling is needed.', 'VS', '2025-04-22 05:26'),
