1. Lead Marketing Analytics (MarTech &amp; Attribution Systems Expert)

Overview
Dina’s team is searching for a highly technical Lead Marketing Analyst with expertise in Marketing Technology (MarTech), advertising platforms, and attribution systems. This role is not focused on traditional marketing analytics but rather on deep technical analysis of marketing performance, requiring knowledge of data modeling, ad platforms, and media mix modeling.

Key Responsibilities:
Oversee marketing analytics strategy, ensuring accurate tracking, reporting, and interpretation of data across multiple digital marketing channels.
Develop and maintain marketing attribution models to analyze the impact of different marketing efforts on overall business performance.
Work with MarTech tools, including Google Ads, Meta Ads, DSPs, DMPs, CDPs, and other ad platforms to ensure efficient data flow and accurate campaign performance tracking.
Implement media mix modeling (MMM) and other advanced statistical techniques to optimize marketing spend.
Collaborate with growth marketing teams, product teams, and finance teams to measure ROI on marketing initiatives.
Ensure compliance with GDPR, CCPA, and other data privacy regulations when handling marketing data.
Develop dashboards and automated reports to monitor marketing KPIs.
Identify opportunities for process automation and enhance data infrastructure related to marketing analytics.
Required Skills &amp; Qualifications:
5+ years of experience in marketing analytics, marketing technology, or digital marketing measurement.
Strong expertise in data analytics, SQL, Python, or R for data modeling and marketing analysis.
Experience working with Google Analytics, Google Ads, Meta Ads Manager, Salesforce, or similar platforms.
Deep understanding of marketing attribution models, including last-click, multi-touch attribution (MTA), and media mix modeling (MMM).
Experience working with big data technologies (Snowflake, BigQuery, AWS Redshift, etc.).
Knowledge of customer segmentation, LTV modeling, and predictive analytics.
Experience in A/B testing and experimental design for marketing performance optimization.
Excellent communication skills and ability to translate complex analytics into actionable insights.
Challenges Noted in Hiring Process:
This position has been open for two months, with some candidates in the final round of interviews.
The ideal candidate needs to be deeply technical and analytical, rather than a traditional agency-style marketing analyst.
2. Lead Member Care &amp; Fraud Analytics (Fraud Prevention &amp; Strategy Expert)

Overview
The second role is a Lead Member Care Analytics &amp; Fraud Prevention Specialist. While it involves traditional customer service analytics, the primary focus is fraud detection and prevention, given the increasing volume of fraud and security threats.

Key Responsibilities:
Lead the Member Care Analytics Team, focusing on fraud detection, prevention, and customer protection strategies.
Develop and implement fraud prevention models, monitoring transaction patterns, anomalies, and suspicious behavior.
Work closely with cybersecurity, compliance, and risk management teams to mitigate fraud risks.
Analyze fraud trends and continuously enhance fraud detection algorithms.
Oversee the integration of fraud detection tools and other risk management technologies.
Develop customer service analytics dashboards and optimize customer support processes based on data insights.
Design and oversee automated risk management workflows to improve fraud detection efficiency.
Stay ahead of industry trends in cyber fraud, identity theft, and payment security.
Collaborate with law enforcement, financial institutions, and cybersecurity professionals to address fraud cases.
Work with the current fraud analyst (a former cybersecurity expert from CrowdStrike) to build out a long-term fraud prevention strategy.
Required Skills &amp; Qualifications:
7+ years of experience in fraud prevention, risk management, or cybersecurity analytics.
Strong background in fraud analytics, data security, and risk assessment.
Expertise in fraud detection tools (e.g., Riskified, Forter, Sift, Feedzai, Cybersource, etc.).
Experience with machine learning models for fraud prevention and risk scoring.
Strong understanding of cyber threat intelligence and financial crime tactics.
Familiarity with regulatory frameworks (KYC, AML, PSD2, GDPR, PCI-DSS).
Proficiency in SQL, Python, or R for fraud analytics and data modeling.
Ability to lead cross-functional teams and work closely with data science, cybersecurity, and legal teams.
Strong analytical and strategic thinking skills.
Previous experience in customer service analytics, fraud risk assessment, and threat mitigation.
Challenges Noted in Hiring Process:
This role is a unique hybrid position, combining elements of cybersecurity, fraud detection, project management, and data analytics.
The fraud landscape has become more aggressive, increasing the demand for a highly skilled fraud prevention specialist.
Dina’s team already has a high-level fraud analyst, but they need a strategic leader to drive long-term fraud prevention efforts.', 'VS', '2025-03-18 06:40'),
