  (144518704320::bigint, 133612170450::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, '19/02 Jeff wrote :

Andy + Team,

Looking forward to our conversation on Monday - sending a pre-read in advance.  Appreciate if you could keep it confidential as we are now in multiple conversations with key stakeholders in the Sports Ecosystem.

For background, we are in the early stages of creating a start-up centered around Sports + AI, working directly with AI foundry Red Cell Partners (detailed in the pre-read).  We’ve outlined our initial thinking – it would be great to get a better understanding of your Team''s capabilities around Technology and AI and explore if there are any points of collaboration.  Would also love any thoughts / feedback on our overall concept and approach to the market.

Thanks and look forward to connecting.
_____________

20/02 John replied 👇:

''''Hi Jeff,

Very interesting read and without a doubt this is a segment of opportunity. As well as a long background in Life Sciences, I also spent 5 years as a CTO in the loyalty industry and there are a number of parallels and threads we should explore as part of that, we also have an expert associate business executive with very deep experience in the commercial side of monetising data through loyalty type schemes across media, retail and travel brands, we can potentially involve him and bring his insight to the table when the time is right.
The immersive opportunities for fan engagement are huge but are still in an experimental stage and on the few engagements where they are done well, it is clear there is a huge amount of heavy lifting behind the scenes. As an example, at a recent England Lionesses game where we hosted clients at Wembley stadium, there was a pre match light and music show where the audience signed up to participate and their phones became part of the show. But the sign up to participate involved a quite lengthy user journey, downloading an app, signing up etc etc. It worked well but undoubtedly there was a heavy lift. And there did not appear to be any real segmentation or understanding who had signed up from which demographic etc, it was simply "scan this QR code if you want to take part".
However, the ability to have a stadium platform where fans are already signed up to get basic value features (travel information, stadium routing to the least busy gate etc etc) but are then offered a variety of content, experience, participation will be a game changer. Not only would it mean that immersive events such as the one I describe above are easy to deploy and not one offs, you also have the fans on the platform for  as well as the ability to reward, incentivise and upsell products and services. And with AI the techniques to identify which users are likely to respond to the best offer or experience become vastly amplified.
So assuming I have grasped the proposition at least partially well, it makes total sense and the player who gets the platform right will have a definite opportunity for success.
From a GT perspective, we can provide business insight and expertise on how best to use data in such a context, we can also back that up with deep architecture and data engineering skills, training and defining the right ML models and ensuring that your Agentic AI solution has optimised data sets to work with. We can do this either by providing resources direct to you or we can operate on a project model where we own a deliverable which we then co govern to ensure you get the outcomes you are seeking. We have a number of relevant use cases that we can share more about when we meet! Looking forward to the discussion.''''', 'VS', '2025-02-19 12:05'),
