  (133736648943::bigint, 117049155800::bigint, null::bigint, 90480899283::bigint, '03/02 CALL NOTES (Chris, Vika, Nikita, Andy, John):

Intro:
The client operates in the building services sector with revenues of around $10–$12 million.
They have a fragmented, legacy technology environment with significant manual processing and overheads.
____________________________________
Chris mentioned 3 Opportunities for the client:
Enhancing and fully integrating the existing CRM system to reduce manual overheads.
Transforming the rich dataset into a sophisticated, AI-powered product that automates forecasting and opens up new revenue channels.
Digitally modernizing a legacy publication and project management tool to create an interactive, subscription-based platform that solidifies the client''s leadership in the construction industry.
1. CRM Integration and Optimization (Sugar CRM)
Overview:
The client currently uses Sugar CRM as the backbone for its customer-related processes. While the system is somewhat integrated into parts of the business (sales, marketing, and billing), many processes remain fragmented and manually driven.

Key Details:
Current State:
Sugar CRM is already in place and integrated to some extent.
The system is seen as functional in certain areas but lacks full, seamless integration across all business processes.
The client faces significant manual processing and overheads due to this fragmented integration.
Opportunity Description:
Enhancement Over Replacement: Rather than completely replacing the CRM (which would be a disruptive and costly overhaul), the recommendation is to leverage the existing system.
Integration Focus: Improve the integration points between the CRM and other operational systems (marketing, billing, and sales processing) to ensure that all business data flows through a central platform.
Process Automation: Automate currently manual processes that are causing overheads. This could involve streamlining data entry, reducing duplicate data handling, and enabling real-time data updates.
Benefits:
Cost-Efficiency: Optimizing an existing system is less expensive than a full system replacement.
Improved Operational Efficiency: Better integration would reduce manual work, lower overheads, and increase the accuracy and timeliness of data.
Foundation for Future Enhancements: A well-integrated CRM sets the stage for future digital transformation projects within the business.
2. Data Product Enhancement Using AI and Machine Learning
Overview:
The client has accumulated a wealth of research data related to building equipment (such as air conditioning units, heat pumps, etc.) gathered by researchers globally. Currently, this data is stored in basic spreadsheets on Office 365 SharePoint, and the potential of this data is underutilized.

Key Details:
Current State:
The data is a result of extensive primary research, involving structured interviews and data capture from manufacturers.
It’s stored in a very basic format (spreadsheets), limiting its current usability.
A proof of concept has already been completed, demonstrating that the data can be used for machine learning-based forecasting.
Opportunity Description:
Immediate Automation: Use machine learning to optimize and automate the existing forecasting process, replacing lengthy manual methods with an automated, data-driven approach.
Product Innovation: Beyond process automation, there is potential to transform this rich dataset into a new digital product. This could include:
Advanced Analytics: Offering predictive analytics and trend forecasting services to customers.
Licensing and Reporting: Creating subscription-based or one-off licensed data reports for industry players, manufacturers, and competitors.
Enhanced Data Integration: Incorporating live data feeds from instrumentation (if applicable in the future) to further enrich the dataset.
Benefits:
Revenue Generation: Unlocking additional value from historical and ongoing data could open up new revenue streams.
Competitive Edge: Using AI/ML to provide more precise and automated forecasting could give the client an advantage over competitors still relying on manual processes.
Customer Value: Enhanced data products can provide deeper insights to both buyers and manufacturers, fostering better decision-making in the construction and building services industry.
3. Digital Transformation of the Publication and Project Management Tool
Overview:
The client currently offers a well-known reference publication for construction project managers and an associated project management tool. Presently, the publication is created in InDesign and distributed as a PDF, while the project management tool exists as an Excel workbook. This opportunity focuses on evolving these traditional tools into a modern digital offering.

Key Details:
Current State:
Publication:
The publication serves as the industry’s go-to guide, updated on a multi-year cycle.
It is currently a static PDF produced using InDesign.
Project Management Tool:
Based on the REBA standard, the tool assigns roles and tasks across different phases of construction.
It’s a basic Excel workbook that lacks the scalability and features expected of a modern project management system.
Opportunity Description:
Digital Modernization:
Convert the static publication into an interactive, digital platform. This may include responsive design, online updates, and integration with other digital tools.
Redesign the project management tool to create a robust, multi-tenant digital platform. This platform could include features such as:
Task and Role Management: Enhanced functionalities for assigning and tracking project responsibilities.
Collaboration Tools: Real-time collaboration features that facilitate communication among teams and contractors.
Subscription Model: Transition from a one-time purchase to a subscription-based service, potentially driving recurring revenue.
Competitive Benchmarking:
Explore similar products in the market (e.g., Chime) to ensure that the digital transformation offers competitive features and pricing.
Broader Product Opportunity:
Leverage the established industry reputation of the current guide to offer additional value-added services and data-driven insights to the construction community.
Benefits:
Revenue Doubling Potential: The new digital product could potentially double the revenue from the current publication and tool.
Market Differentiation: A modern, interactive platform could strengthen the client''s position as the industry standard.
Enhanced User Experience: An improved digital experience can drive higher customer engagement and satisfaction.
Scalability: A digital platform provides the opportunity for continuous updates, integration of new features, and expansion into additional markets or services.
Client Stakeholders:
Lisa Ashworth (CEO):
Leading the transformation effort as a long-term strategic initiative (not a short-term exit strategy).
Kim Burgess (didn''t find her on Linkedin):
Involved in operational/product discussions, serving in a contract capacity.
NEXT STEPS:
Further meetings are planned (initially via Teams) to refine the scope and gather more detailed requirements.
Proposal Preparation:
Vika: Proposal for Business Analysis/Solution Design phase and subsequent development phases including wireframes and architectural plans.
Confirm if the client is open to dedicating part of the budget for this preparatory work.
Team Coordination:
Andy to lead the technical and project oversight, with potential integration of external executives for senior guidance.
Chris to follow up with the client after an upcoming meeting to communicate any decisions and set up further Teams calls. Chris meets tomorrow (Tue, 4th of Feb) with the client’s project team. In this meeting, he plans to discuss a different topic—specifically, he mentioned that he had looked over the specification (for one of the opportunities) and would be meeting them to talk further about it.
Client Communication:
Ensure that key stakeholders (Lisa Ashworth, Kim Burgess) are updated on progress and the planned approach.
Schedule a follow-up meeting (in-person when necessary) once there is clarity on the project’s scope and budget allocation.', 'VS', '2025-02-03 08:38'),
