  (37073909187::bigint, 16179571915::bigint, null::bigint, 13316065012::bigint, '01/10 Offline meeting in OCL Vision;s Office:

John''s from OCL visit for the system and to feed the proposal: Nik Rudge
Mark - head of operations    Ben - head of finance
Darren Millington - helping on a transactionAndy
JohnNik - context, we are a small business that would like to be a bigger business, we are right in the middle of an investment process right now
We have a done of data, we think there is value in it, we have neither the time, reosurce or expertise to know what that lokos like. Primarily we hope to grow revenue - patient acquisition, patient conversion etc. But thats partly because thats what we know so there could be more in it...
3 sites currently
We think value comes more through revenue than through data to cut costs....
If we can show a return on the work we do then it becomes very easy...So we don’t know whats possible, see what we can do and discover, and then whether its immediate or with a future investor, with us as a partner lined up etc....Andy - how old is the data
System switched over in June last year...
Virtual servers hosted in GermanyAndy - once data is sorted, segmented, cleaned... then a case of building the LLMs etc...
And potentially productising some of this. You then hit a fork in the road, are you going to be a product company, are you ready to ideate round prodcut etc?Mark
Hubspot as our CRM. Biggest issue is the legacy systems, different systems not finishing the communication off with each other....
Compucare - where the information goes for consultation and appointment management
Medisite - clinical patient management infromation system (patient record)Hubspot connects to google, lets us see what lead generation coming through
Hunspot speaks to Compucare a litutle bit, knows when an appointment is happening
Medisite, one way comms, gets the patient data....
THen finance system stand alone, no linkage there.... Zero is our financiing system, recognises invoices generated in Compucare and reconciles themWant to get the data all into one lake, show me the person, and the full picture, do we already know them, single view of the customer, someone may already know OCL but then may be coming in for a different enquiry, etc etc...Nik the super secret source is patient conversion and acquisition
We are really good at front of house, ie when you call us and say you want x procedure from y surgeon, when can you book me in then we are great.
But what we are less good at is having a conversation about the fact that there are 2 top surgeons available on the day you wanted and one is top 5 in the world, thats a selling tool....
Ability to be able to know that someone was referred by someone was a patient,So the customer journey is a key aspect of this....
And the existing architecture of multiple platforms,
Each meets an existing need... but no enterprise architecture...
No middleware in place, the bridges that have been made are a very rough and ready interface database....
So if something is wrong in the middleware, it then needs correcting in the database manual - real single point of failure....Darren - very robust dashboard would be great, to show what the key performance indicators areJH - suggested architecture review- get the right middleware AND create a data lake....THen good discussion about how you would use the data lake, can you spot the surgeons with more free slots, how would you then offer the pricing options and reductions on a targeted basis...
Nik - so building out some personas - a 28 year old from Essex really likely to respond to a discount offer than a Mayfair 45 year old....Architect review
Andrew Muzelle involvement and engagement
Then create and engineer the right kind of data lake and middelware to drive the value...V similar to the loyalty program challenges, its about segmentation etAndy - whats the patient journey?
comes in via a weblead or to th website, try and get call back or email within 15 minutes....
Enquiries done online
Booking has to be done manually today , cant manage to do online web booking ( said it was becasue of Compucare, not sure if that is the way they have deployed COmpucare or a restriction in Compucare itself....). Compucare has as web solution BUT it needs a very clear and robust process to then deploy the online booking....
Conversion from out patient to surgeon is about 67% although there is variation between surgeons which is an interesting data point in itself45% of enquiries turn into consultations, 67% of thsoe turn into surgeries... if we could get those both up 10% that would be huge....The medical secretaries are great at talking about the procedures, but the conversion option is less good....,
Example - someone looking at pricing first then surgeons probably goes down this path.... or someone looking at CQC report first probably has a quality mindset and wants to ensure that safety and quality is key
And things like the complication rate for each surgeon for a certain procedure, that could be key information that patients might ask etc etc....Private medical or insurance tie ups?
Yes, registered with all of the major players, Bupa etc... And can we start to measure what comes from where? And then have a marketing strategy to show the payers the quality of offering etc etc and where its differentiated etc....Andy
Workstream one - the right data analyst / engineer does it have to be Power BI or are there other options? (Darren made clear that not committed yet to PowerBI or Tableau so there is some choice)d
so getting the data into a robust shape, get that hygiene step done
Build out a data dashbaord to give you that real time visibility into whats there
That wont show you what we dont know yet, but the new KPIs could build out, like inter site efficiency and productivity on yield and pricing
Workstream two in parallel
architecture review which optimises the middleware against the desired patient journey
Then you start looking at teh price optimisation, funnel optimisation, etc in the roadmap, feels like there is a demographic out there that will want to be totally digital, doesnt mean that we will remove the human touch for those that want it..... (this is the Andrew Muzelle phase)Andy also had some thoughts on dynamic pricing, actually better gold would be fill order book for 6 weeks ahead at full price and full schedule.... Once you go down the promo discount route its hard to back out of that...CISO - do you have one ?
