  (36268089061::bigint, null::bigint, 31593297392::bigint, 13479224545::bigint, 'Chris Watkins works at Biodesix as Director of Information Technology for 9 years.
Based in the Denver Metropolitan Area, he plays a pivotal role in managing the company''s IT infrastructure, overseeing systems that support Biodesix’s data-driven diagnostic solutions. His responsibilities involve the strategic planning and management of IT resources to enhance the company’s operational efficiency, focusing on secure data handling, which is critical for their lung cancer diagnostic services. His prior experience as an IT Infrastructure Manager at DaVita Kidney Care has given him extensive expertise in healthcare-related technology operations​.

Company overview:
Biodesix is a diagnostic solutions company focused on providing data-driven tests primarily for lung diseases, such as lung cancer and COVID-19. The company uses a unique combination of multi-omics, including genomics and proteomics, alongside artificial intelligence (AI) to develop blood-based diagnostic tests.
Founded in 2005 and headquartered in Boulder, Colorado, the company uses a unique combination of multi-omics, including genomics and proteomics, alongside artificial intelligence (AI) to develop blood-based diagnostic tests. Its flagship products include the Nodify Lung® and IQLung™ test strategies. These tests provide critical insights into nodule risk assessment and lung cancer treatment decisions, speeding up the diagnosis and treatment process for patients. In particular, the Nodify XL2® and Nodify CDT® tests assess malignancy risk in pulmonary nodules, while the GeneStrat® and VeriStrat® tests help oncologists guide personalized treatment for lung cancer​.
Biodesix is notable for offering five Medicare-covered diagnostic tests for lung disease and for collaborating with major biotechnology companies to enhance its diagnostic offerings through the use of advanced AI models.

Technology Stack and Job Openings
Biodesix’s technology infrastructure is driven by its Diagnostic Cortex® AI platform, which powers its multi-omic diagnostic tests by combining data from different biological levels (proteins, genes, etc.) to provide faster and more accurate diagnostics.
Key technologies include Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS), digital droplet PCR (ddPCR), and multi-omics integration for complex data analysis. 
The company frequently recruits professionals in bioinformatics, data science, software engineering, and AI/machine learning to support its technology infrastructure.
Recent job postings emphasize expertise in programming languages like Python and R, cloud-based systems for data storage, and platforms that facilitate the integration of machine learning models​.

Recent News and Partnerships:
Partnerships: In 2024, Biodesix announced an expanded collaboration with Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center (MSK) to co-develop oncology biomarker assays, leveraging Bio-Rad’s digital PCR technology. This partnership builds on their work in the field of oncology diagnostics​.
Inc. Magazine Recognition: In 2024, Biodesix was named to Inc. Magazine''s 5000 list of fastest-growing companies, reflecting its consistent growth in the lung diagnostics market.
Financial Performance: Biodesix raised its full-year sales guidance after a strong second quarter in 2024, driven by increasing demand for its lung diagnostics solutions. This performance is credited to improved revenue from its lung nodule management tests. The company is on track for further growth, buoyed by expanding partnerships and strategic investments​.
Financial Performance and Capital Expenditure (2023-2024)
In 2023 and 2024, Biodesix experienced solid financial growth, largely attributed to the increased adoption of its lung diagnostics solutions. The company reported strong second-quarter results for 2024, surpassing analysts'' expectations with improved revenue from lung disease diagnostics. As a result, Biodesix raised its full-year revenue guidance, which boosted investor confidence.
Capital expenditures have been focused on scaling their Diagnostic Cortex® platform and enhancing R&amp;D efforts to support the development of new diagnostic solutions. The company also recently completed a stock offering to raise $17.4 million, which will help fund future growth and development initiatives', 'AM', '2024-09-27 05:34'),
