Company Overview:
Pramana is a health technology company, spun out of nference, that focuses on advancing digital pathology through AI and automation. Their key offering is Digital Pathology as a Service (DPaaS), which allows medical centers and pathology labs to digitize their pathology slides for analysis without needing significant capital investment. This service integrates both hardware and software for efficient slide scanning, particularly in the fields of anatomic pathology, cytology, and microbiology​


Products overview:

Spectral Family of Solutions: Pramana''s line of digital pathology solutions is centered on creating high-quality whole slide images (WSI) with AI-enhanced features like pixel-level z-stacking. Their systems automate many processes traditionally done manually, such as quality control, focusing, and error detection.
Digital Pathology as a Service (DPaaS): This model is designed to reduce costs and barriers to adopting digital pathology by offering a flexible, pay-per-slide service. This system allows labs to digitize slides without long-term commitments​

Technology and Software Overview:
Pramana’s technology focuses on Digital Pathology 2.0, which leverages AI and real-time error detection to generate high-quality, standardized images for pathology labs. Their software uses DICOM and OME-TIFF formats to ensure interoperability with other imaging systems.

Recent News and Partnerships

1st of October - webinar: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/pramana-digital-pathology_digitalpathology-ironmountain-pramana-activity-7244705006149332992-nbrD?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop 

Business Challenges:
Pramana faces the challenge of converting a traditionally manual and capital-intensive pathology workflow to a fully digital one. Despite the benefits, less than 10% of pathology labs have adopted digital systems, mainly due to cost and skepticism about image quality. By addressing these issues through automation and AI-driven solutions, Pramana aims to drive greater adoption of digital pathology​', 'VS', '2024-09-27 05:18'),
