  (35700569302::bigint, null::bigint, 31590364094::bigint, 13479366365::bigint, 'Contact overview:

Anne Stoker is the Chief Operating Officer at Millar, Inc., a company specializing in medical sensor technology. He joined Millar in 1997 as a senior design/manufacturing engineer and has held various roles including Product Manager and Director of Manufacturing. Before joining Millar, Anne began her career at Sentron, a manufacturer of pressure sensor solutions. He holds a Bachelor''s degree in Mechanical Engineering and has played a key role in advancing Millar’s operations and product development, particularly in pressure sensor technology​.

Company Overview:

Millar specializes in medical pressure sensor technology, offering innovative solutions for OEM medical devices. They focus on precision pressure measurements and advancing medical research through high-performance sensors.

Products overview:

Millar offers products like Mikro-Cath™ pressure catheters and OEM pressure sensor solutions for clinical, research, and OEM applications.

Technology and Software Overview:

Millar’s software primarily supports real-time data acquisition and analysis, working in tandem with their pressure sensor technologies. Their software stack is designed to integrate with MEMS-based sensors and catheters like the Mikro-Cath™, enabling users to monitor physiological parameters with precision. The software provides data visualization, reporting tools, and supports wireless communication for remote monitoring. It is widely used in clinical research and medical device integration, focusing on seamless connectivity with their hardware solutions for comprehensive data-driven insights.

Recent News and Partnerships:

Key challenges may include maintaining innovation leadership in sensor technology, addressing regulatory requirements, and competing in the growing med-tech market.

Business Challenges:

Recent news from Millar Inc. highlights several strategic moves and innovations in the medical sensor industry. Notably, in November 2023, Millar announced its acquisition of Sentron, a Netherlands-based company specializing in pressure and pH sensors. This acquisition will allow Millar to become a comprehensive provider of sensor development, enhancing its capacity to create pressure and pH monitoring systems for medical and research applications.

Additionally, in October 2023, Millar unveiled its new chronic pressure measurement platform at the MD&amp;M Minneapolis event. This innovation is set to provide advanced solutions for continuous pressure monitoring, further establishing Millar''s leadership in MEMS-based sensor technology​.

Partnership:

ADInstruments: Millar has a long-standing partnership with ADInstruments, a global provider of data acquisition systems for life sciences research. Through this collaboration, Millar’s Mikro-Tip® Pressure Catheters are distributed alongside ADInstruments'' systems, providing comprehensive solutions for cardiovascular and pulmonary research​.

Sentron: In 2023, Millar acquired Sentron, a Netherlands-based manufacturer of pressure and pH sensors. This acquisition broadens Millar’s portfolio, adding pH sensor technologies to their existing MEMS-based pressure sensors​.

Transonic Scisense: Millar has also partnered with Transonic Scisense to integrate their pressure-volume loop technology, combining the strengths of both companies to enhance physiological monitoring and hemodynamic research​.', 'VS', '2024-09-24 06:21'),
  (35697637351::bigint, null::bigint, 31592340419::bigint, 13477709804::bigint, 'Annika has worked at ABC Medical for 8+ years and started Head of Operations Systems and Information Technology position in 2023.

In 2024, Annika is expected to continue focusing on further digital transformation initiatives. These efforts include improving ABC Medical’s customer relationship management (CRM) systems and enhancing the use of data analytics to optimize the supply chain and improve customer service. One of her key areas of responsibility is implementing secure and scalable IT systems to support the growing volume of patients and healthcare providers the company serves​

