Software Components:
Mobile Application:
Bluetooth Connectivity:
Data Tracking and Analytics:
User Interface (UI):
Cloud Infrastructure (potentially evolving):
Recent News and Partnerships:

Recently, Koya Medical has made significant strides in expanding its influence in the healthcare industry, particularly focusing on treatments for lymphedema and venous diseases. In November 2023, the company closed a financing round of up to $30 million led by OrbiMed, a prominent healthcare investment firm. This funding is intended to support the continued growth and commercialization of Koya’s Dayspring system, an active compression therapy designed to improve mobility and quality of life for those suffering from lymphedema and chronic venous insufficiency. The additional capital will help the company expand its product development, clinical research, and efforts to broaden the indications for its therapy​.

Earlier in 2022, Koya Medical raised $26 million in Series B funding, with investments from firms like 3x5 Partners and Asahi Kasei Ventures. This round was pivotal for advancing the Dayspring system''s commercialization and clinical research. The device stands out for being FDA-cleared and enabling patient mobility during treatment, a significant departure from traditional, more restrictive therapies​.

These financial boosts are part of Koya Medical’s broader strategy to address unmet needs in the treatment of lymphatic and venous disorders, conditions that affect millions of people but remain under-served in the medical device market​

