Enhance your ability to collaborate effectively within remote teams, leveraging your experience to contribute to our inclusive and supportive work environment.
About you:
You have a solid foundation in TypeScript and are comfortable writing automated test cases with it.
You bring at least 5 years of experience in mobile-focused QA automation.
You demonstrate expertise in Appium, Jest, WebDriverIO, and BrowserStack, ensuring a robust testing framework.
Your strong skills in test case design and GitHub management enable efficient test execution and reporting.
You have experience with mobile app deployment via App Store Connect and Google Play, facilitating seamless integration of testing processes.
Bonus points:
You are interested in exploring additional automation tools and technologies to further enhance our testing capabilities.
You have experience working with error tracking tools like Sentry, enriching our ability to identify and address issues promptly.
You are passionate about contributing to a mission-driven organisation and are excited to play a key role in transforming human connections through technology.', 'VS', '2024-09-17 08:45'),
  (34142483173::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, 7667816934::bigint, 'Current DMs:
Andrew Sadler - CPTO @ Castor
Derk Arts - Founder and CEO

About
Castor is a leading provider of decentralized and hybrid clinical trial solutions. The company''s primary goal is to transform clinical research by making it more patient-centric, mobile, and data-driven. Castor offers a cloud-based platform that enables researchers to easily capture and integrate data from various sources, including electronic health records (EHR), to streamline and accelerate the trial process. Its platform supports real-world data collection, eConsent, ePRO (patient-reported outcomes), and electronic data capture (EDC), serving over 14,000 studies across 90 countries. Castor has gained recognition for its ability to modernize clinical trials and is known for working with clients like the World Health Organization on COVID-19 studies​.

Technology Needs and Stack
Castor’s platform is designed to be highly scalable, enabling the rapid deployment of decentralized clinical trials. The platform integrates EHRs with data capture solutions, facilitating seamless data collection. It focuses heavily on mobile data strategies and interoperability to improve trial efficiency. Castor’s tech team is continuously expanding, with ongoing hiring for roles like clinical development officers, and a focus on integrating AI-driven capabilities into clinical trials. The company is also interested in expanding its software development for enhanced trial management​.

Recent News and Partnerships:Castor raised $45 million in a Series B funding round, led by Eight Roads Ventures and F-Prime Capital, which brought its total funding to $65 million. The company is using this investment to expand globally, with a focus on the U.S. and Asia-Pacific regions, enhancing product development, and hiring top talent. 

The World Health Organization (WHO) has also partnered with Castor for its Solidarity trial, a major project aimed at finding COVID-19 treatments, which has helped further solidify Castor''s presence in decentralized clinical trials. Additionally, Castor is working with some of the largest pharmaceutical companies and digital therapeutic firms, emphasizing its role in shaping the future of decentralized, patient-centered trials​.

Business Challenges:Managing the vast amounts of data generated in decentralized trials, ensuring data integrity and compliance with stringent privacy laws like GDPR and HIPAA, and staying ahead of competition in a fast-evolving market. Competitors like Medidata, Clario, and ICON are also innovating rapidly in the decentralized clinical trial space. Furthermore, the adoption of new digital solutions by conservative stakeholders in the medical field can be slow, presenting a barrier to more widespread implementation​.
Additionally, scaling their infrastructure to support increasingly complex trials, particularly in global markets with varying regulatory requirements, will remain a significant hurdle as the company grows.', 'AM', '2024-09-16 04:39'),
