  (33256857018::bigint, 16160214231::bigint, null::bigint, 13291113194::bigint, 'John''s Notes: 

Dan West - CIO at Dreams, a major retailer across the UK, owned by a major US company, Tempur Sealy. I know Dan from Aimia days where he was CIO of Nectar Card. Steve West now works direct for Dan and has brought us into Dreams and I met with them last week. They have multiple needs, basically more projects than staff but need a level of discipline injecting into their decision making and generation of business cases. At the minute there is a lot of poor behaviour where business departments go off and find their own solutions. An immediate need is for a combination of business analysis and architecture as a service, where we could provide a capability to look at a need or set of requirements, do the analysis on business case and then come back with recommended costed package options. There may also be the possibility of us placing MS Dynamics folks in the future to replace some very expensive consultants he currently has, he needs them for now as they are finishing a major deployment, but once they move to steady state he will want to take out some costs. 
