  (32034736316::bigint, 15427203046::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, '29/08 CALL NOTES:

Dennis, Lori, and Rob thank you for taking the time to meet with us. It was great to hear about your current projects and understand your needs better. We''re excited about the opportunity to collaborate and provide the support you need.
Brian, appreciate sharing the Mpower tech stack doc. We''ll start studying it ASAP.
As agreed, I''d like to send the follow-up with the key points and next steps that we agreed on today:


1. Potential paths for engagement:
CRM Integration and Platform Review: we managed to discuss the priority of enhancing your internal workflows and the platform, considering the complexities and potential future-proofing required.
Discovery Phase: we agreed that the next step should be a focused Discovery Phase to assess either the migration of your current ordering system to Microsoft Dynamics or further improvements to your client portal and Mpower system.
2. Discovery Phase Overview:
GT will provide a Business Analyst, Delivery Manager, and Software Solution Architect who will work closely with your team.
The Discovery Phase will last around ~1 month, requiring your participation, particularly from Dennis, to provide access to systems and infrastructure.
This phase aims to define project scope, timelines, and costs for future delivery.
3. Next Steps:
Mspark will have an internal discussion and confirm which path to prioritize for the Discovery Phase,
Mspark will share additional materials/requirements so we can roughly estimate the scope of work and have a better understanding of the main goal of the Discovery Phase,
GT will share the MSA and Service Schedule agreement for the initial Discovery Phase (will try to share them with you before our next call starts),
Mspark and GT will have weekly syncs to align on the project goals, timelines, and required resources.
To keep momentum, how about booking a slot in our calendar every Wednesday at 9:00 am your time to have Mspark &amp; GT weekly syncs? Would it work well for you?', 'VS', '2024-08-30 03:35'),
