  (27786763240::bigint, null::bigint, 3353254127::bigint, null::bigint, 'PhD focused in Medicine from University of Cambridge (2004-2009)
Skilled in Innovation Management, Oncology, Molecular Biology, Patent Law, and Biotechnology.
CEO and Co-founder at Start Codon 
Start Codon - an accelerator based in Cambridge, England. The firm is a pre and seed-stage venture capital fund that runs a business venture building and accelerator program. The firm seeks to invest in disruptive healthcare and life science companies.
Has made 5 investments:
2023 - NK:IO (a biotech company that develops novel approaches to natural killer cell-mediated immunotherapy);
2022 - coding.bio (ML-Based Design of CAR-T Cell Therapies)
2021 - Enhanc3D Genomics (Developer of a biotechnology platform designed to develop tools for large-scale analysis of genetic variations and gene function. The company''s technology specializes in profiles of three-dimensional genome folding at high resolution for all genes and their enhancers simultaneously, enabling researchers to focus on the advancement of novel drugs in areas of unmet medical needs)
2020 - Spirea (is committed to delivering the next generation of Antibody Drug Conjugate (ADC) therapeutics to revolutionise cancer treatment and improve the lives of patients)
2020 - Semarion (everages microfabrication technology to build smart materials and develop novel cell assaying applications)
Start Codon''s investment strategy appears to focus on early-stage life science startups, with a strong emphasis on biotechnology and therapeutics. The firm shows a preference for companies that are part of the health care, science, and engineering sectors. Geographically, there is a clear inclination towards entities based in the United Kingdom, with a particular interest in those located within the Cambridge Cluster, although they have also invested in companies from other prominent academic hubs such as London and Oxford. The investments are typically not lead investments, suggesting a strategy of participating alongside other investors rather than spearheading funding rounds. Companies that might be attractive to Start Codon for future investment would likely be innovative startups within the life sciences domain, especially those engaged in biotechnology and therapeutic development, and preferably based in the UK''s prominent academic and research centers.', 'AM', '2024-05-13 08:50'),
  (27786502102::bigint, null::bigint, 3345592515::bigint, 10759150819::bigint, 'LN BIO:
I have been leading éclateral since co-founding it in 2020. We have raised £2M to date to deliver... home testing with clinical confidence with the most accessible and affordable digitally connected home testing diagnostic platform.
Left Avacta Life Sciences in March 2017 and started metaLinear Ltd in order to focus on identifying new diagnostic and therapeutic targets in certain disease areas using Affimer® technology (Next-generation biotherapeutics to surpass the limitations of cancer therapies).
PhD in Biochemistry, focussed on protein phosphorylation/signal transduction/cell cycle control
Post-doc in yeast genetics, focussing on signal transduction and nuclear transport
Established the Peptide Aptamer Group in the MRC Cancer Cell Unit in Cambridge, UK (2001-2007)
Leader of the Peptide Aptamer Group in the Leeds Institute of Molecular Medicine (LIMM) (since 2007)
Founder, Aptuscan Ltd, May 2008 (acquired by Avacta)
Social media activity:
April, 2024 - Fantastic to have been at the Medilink South West Innovation Awards last night with these three people from the éclateral team.
April, 2024 - a guest on podcast. Really invigorating interview with Johnny Isaacs yesterday. My first podcast, but made all the easier by the background work he’d put in.
éclateral - Developer of diagnostic test kits designed to empower people to carry out tests at home with clinical professionals diagnosing remotely.
specializes in underpinning improvements in diagnostics and testing for consumers, healthcare professionals and clinical trials, tethered data flow enables home testing with clinical confidence by allowing each result to be assessed by a clinician before the result is shared with the patient.
Products:
o~pal: a portable solution for rapid health testing, app, reader
