  (26439840443::bigint, 11801872369::bigint, null::bigint, 7667791090::bigint, '04/04 CALL NOTES

Rachel is off till 15th of April

Rachel - joined 10 months ago. She is Head of data and MA in Machine Learning, heading up data, machine learning and product.

When we worked with Dean did some work on the large-scale entity resolution problem we were facing. Intiial work we did was a good prototyping exercise but its actually a very difficutl problem to solve.
See this in the market
recently did some work with Ernst and Young, they gave feedback that Zeki were in the top 5 firms in the approach to large enttiy resolution
Some of the work we did had contributed ot it. Dean and team went thruogh lots of iterations approaching how we did things. That has been trasnformative, its the lynchpin on how we bring all the data sets together
So at the moment deploying product on top of that data
Built out front end UI based tool which lets people search and retrieve that data
Going live on snowflake soon
And now able to deploy large scale data on other peoples platforms
Just got off a call with Blackrock around how we could be a stream into one of their prodcuts
A lot of interest from government and other customersWaiting for next phase of customer feebdack before we do next phase of developmentGot paying customers for reports and for data cubes, ie CSV files that gets deployed to a cloud spaceGot a discovery product built to MVP, looking at investing in that next based on the feedback from customers.So what we are looking to do at the minute is figure out how to talk the discovery product to next level once we have the feedback. Talking to pther providers on whether we can completely outsource it or whether we do an augmented approach...So could we outsource it to a specific backlog, whats our business model in that sense......TEam mainly in houseHas expeirence in working with offhsore teams.
Mainly in Serbia.
Want to avoid work going out and being invisible for a large period of time.
Key to success is very close relationship with the product manager, decisions being driven product down,
Want to get the right customer feedback and not to over engineerConceives that an outsource of hte discovery project is what they woudl want to do.....What do we have in terms of Jango expertise, front end Vue JS etc..We have tlaked to a couple of other people, they pride themselves at getting the top 1% etc.Will sned over example skillsets and we can send back the quote.Key is the attitude, ability to make trade offs, display agility to get to the business goal etc...Some dicussion around wanting an outsource model, seems to be that they want outsource as in not augmenting and working with current team. So descrinbed how we could have a dedicated ETM team headed by a delivery team. then governend by Zeki etc...
NEXT STEPS:
Rachel will send job descriptions and scenarios and quote etc...(asked her about Dean, he has left the org, she wasn’t v forthcoming, sounds like he may nto have been successful which is why we are back in the game....?)', 'VS', '2024-04-05 03:41'),
