  (24511744988::bigint, 10906140117::bigint, null::bigint, 10030200290::bigint, '13/02 CALL NOTES (Christophe, Ken, Mike, John, Vika)

About Christophe - Christoph''s focus in consulting at the moment is very much data-driven, commercial data, run scientific data, and that he shared with us a lot of people. Christoph has a rich history in consulting, delivering IT solutions, and data-driven IT solutions or products throughout his career. He has worked in strategic consulting, ensuring the execution of strategies was appropriate or driven by remediation in various scenarios. He has served as a board member of Ensign in France after working with Ken at PA Consulting in London. Christoph''s role involved running data-centered departments in France and reporting for the affiliate in America, highlighting his leadership in managing complex data operations.

Christoph founded his own company, which he later sold to IQVIA (formerly QuintilesIMS), indicating his entrepreneurial spirit and success in creating valuable data-driven solutions in the healthcare and pharmaceutical sectors. He was instrumental in inventing an MDM solution capable of integrating pharmaceutical molecules worldwide into a single repository, showcasing his innovative approach to data integration and management. I was head or practice head for the entire technology group in France within an expertise group of 400 people based in Paris and at least 800 people based in India.

PAIN POINT: struggling to get a good enough team to put together a new product together.

MAIN POINT OF CONVERSATION:
Christoph shared his ideas about the future, including integrating more data and applying AI as part of the data stack to enhance the value derived from aggregated data, reflecting his forward-thinking approach to data consulting and solution development. Christoph is in the early stages of collaboration with Manga Bay, aiming to diversify and enhance their capabilities in data aggregation and analysis. He stressed the importance of building a strong relationship with Manga Bay and securing funding for future projects. The project seeks to move beyond traditional BI systems to more predictive and AI-driven solutions, providing strategic insights and decision support at the board level.

ABOUT PROJECT: He expressed interest in developing a product that integrates commercial data, run scientific data, and applies AI to create a more valuable data stack. This product aims to support strategic decision-making and offer predictive insights. The project seeks to move beyond traditional BI systems to more predictive and AI-driven solutions, providing strategic insights and decision support at the board level. 

NEXT STEPS:
Vika sent the GT LifeScience presentation,
Christophe should send the more information and materials, some API and ideas,
Once Christophe has a better vision of the project, we can continue our discussion on MVP development.', 'VS', '2024-02-14 05:20'),
  (24491171306::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, 9705043677::bigint, '13/02 CALL NOTES (Kathrin, Hajar, John, Ken, Vika)

Hajar Mozaffar - Senior Lecturer in innovation from the Business School, University of Edinburgh. Her own research is basically, there are different lines of research that she covers. One is role of users in digital innovation. The other one is digital transformation of organisations. and that''s what she teaches at the Business School, Digital Transformation.
Broadly, she have worked in many different industries, but for the past decade, her main focus has been on healthcare. She has been working with Catherine very closely on many different projects around digital health. Hajar is also the program director for our master''s program in innovation and entrepreneurship. And I think that''s one of the main reasons that I''m here today. So it''s a master''s program. It''s a one-year master program with very diverse types of students coming from many different backgrounds in terms of geography, but also in terms of, you know, their sort of undergrad degrees. So, they''re here to do a master''s program on innovation and entrepreneurship.

Hajar provided details about the master''s program in innovation and entrepreneurship at the University of Edinburgh for students:
Program Duration and Structure: It''s a 1-year master''s program that starts in May and ends in mid-August. The program includes diverse students from various geographical backgrounds and academic disciplines.
Research Focus: The program covers various lines of research, including the role of users in digital innovation and the digital transformation of organizations. Haja''s focus has been mainly on healthcare for the past decade.
Dissertation Period: Students begin working on their projects in May, with final assignments due in mid-August. This period allows them to conduct a piece of research on a topic of interest.
Student Projects: Most students come into the program with their own project ideas, but they can also approach supervisors for project suggestions in areas like digital transformation, AI, and health tech.
Ethics Consideration: The program aims to align projects with level two ethics, suggesting a preference for projects that do not involve direct interaction with patients or vulnerable groups.
Interest in AI and Health Tech: There is a significant interest among students in projects related to AI and health tech, with Haja currently working on projects in these areas.
Collaboration Potential: The program offers opportunities for students to work on real-world projects, potentially collaborating with companies like GT Life Sciences. This collaboration could involve qualitative research, market analysis, and evaluation of innovation in health tech.

NEXT STEPS
Kathrin should send some materials,
Hajar will talk to 1-2 students to ask about their passion, occupation, and interests.', 'VS', '2024-02-13 12:17'),
  (24278709747::bigint, 9757243344::bigint, null::bigint, 9193875167::bigint, '06/02 CALL NOTES (Kiran, John, Vika):

Kiran''s background: he''s Technology and Business Executive with more than 25 years experience leading technology strategy for small to large companies.

For the last 20 months he worked for Pendulum Therapeutics, which is a biotech startup based in San Francisco. He was leading their Data and Analytics strategy, making sure they use data for making all the business decisions that they need to make and prior to he was there until December, 2023 so now he''s looking for his next opportunity.

Prior to Pendulum he worked for Petco which is a retailer here in US for almost five years so I have a really data and analytics kind of background with a focus on consumer analytics. So essentially looking at a lot of customer data, making sure you understand customer and customer lifetime value, customer and marketing analytics, those sort of things. And also a lot of background with technology specifically in the big data space, modern data and analytics, cloud-based analytics, AI and machine learning. So, a lot of biotech or pharmaceutical companies are basically looking for using data and analytics for drug discovery and other areas, right? And that takes a lot of technology infrastructure, essentially. So that''s where I can provide that expertise. So I consider myself as a business problem solver. So when a problem needs to be solved, typically these days you use digital technology, so that''s where my expertise is.

He''s in active stage of searching the job in San Francisco or San Diego.

Pendulum: they manufacture probiotic supplements and sell that probiotic supplements directly to consumer using their own website, as well as through Amazon and other channels, and also trying to expand with other B2B opportunities using healthcare professionals, HCPs we call it, as well as some wholesalers through which they were trying to sell this probiotic supplement. So the first product they had launched was really for glucose control, essentially people with type 2 diabetes, their products are based on microbiome science.

About Pendulum:
1- Acronymsia -  the first one was for diabetes, then they launched a couple of other products.
2- Metabolic Daily - they have launched three or four different products.
3- Another project - was supposed to be launched, GLP one related at the end of last year, actually October, and that they had postponed that launch. So that actually kind of had an impact on the cash flow situation and they''re having some legal dispute as well related to a patent with one of the companies in Europe. That is the reason, you know, they had to change some of the plans and that''s where they had a restructuring that''s the reason I ended up you know as part of that restructuring left pendulum at the end of last year.

Pendulum will focus on the business issues, which is the patent, as well as securing more funding. So they are backed by good venture capitalists like Sequoia Capital, Cosla Ventures. So they do have backing of good venture capitalists. I don''t think they will invest that much on AI.', 'VS', '2024-02-06 11:14'),
