  (24110368754::bigint, 10634261704::bigint, null::bigint, 9769151419::bigint, '01/02 CALL NOTES (Jeff, Andy, Vika)

Intro: Chris Card introduced us to Jeff, as he asked him about that. Jeff Kim - President of HUMAX Digital, responsible for global business and sales and marketing. Previously, he was the president of Humex Europe, managing European business. He''s more business person and he lives between the UK and Korea (every 2 months). Jeff has his family in the UK.

HUMAX was founded in 1989 initially focused on factory automation.
In 1996, HUMAX launched its first digital set-top box in Europe, later shifting to Humex-branded products in the European retail market around 2000.
At its peak, HUMAX''s global revenue was about $2 billion, primarily from set-top boxes and broadband gateways.
HUMAX has supplied products for various services like Freeview Play in the UK and worked with operators like Virgin Media and Liberty Global.
HUMAX has been known for delivering various types of digital TV solutions globally, including working with AT&amp;T and DirectTV.
Business changes:
About ten years ago, Humex began exploring the automotive business by acquiring Korean companies, focusing on in-vehicle infotainment devices for global OEMs like General Motors, Opel, and Renault-Nissan.
Although they divested this business, they retained insights and inspiration from the automotive sector.
Humex still maintains its automotive antenna business.
In recent years, Humex has shifted focus to mobility services, particularly in Korea. This includes owning parking operators, operating as a Charge Point Operator (CPO), developing EV chargers, and offering car-sharing services.
15 years ago had a polish offshore company
Vietman again, failure.

NEED: offshore product development, external EU partner to complement HUMAX''s internal R&amp;D. HUMAX faces challenges in hiring good engineers in Korea, particularly in firmware engineering. The company aims to innovate by collaborating with companies that have high skill sets and efficiency in software development. HUMAX is focusing on EV charging and home energy management solutions, aiming to provide end-to-end solutions that integrate EV chargers, solar panels, inverters, home batteries, and V2G vehicles.

Who will manage this team? - Need to think about what could be the most efficient way.  EU team - business modeling, product planning. Tech resources are in Korea.

IMPORTANT THINGS FOR JEFF:
good quality of engineering resources (NOT CHEAP),
way of innovation !!!!,
consistency &amp; contingency,
the view of product planning (how to satisfy the customers, identify the pain points, create the new business model, to have a helicopter view).

NEW PROJECT:
Jeff is in charge of EB charging business, energy management business. Primarily want to become - company end to end for home management solution. They started planning the business model, clarifing the real products &amp; key feature in February- March. Jeff would like to start with small team of 4-5 people and then to allocate more engineers. Product''s timeline: ~12 months.

3 business areas:
Firmware Engineers embedded),
Intelligent Back-end side (like charge point management software, CPMS),
Mobile application.

NEXT STEPS:
Vika to prepare the share the marketing presentation with Jeff,
Jeff will have the internal conversation/debate with board team next weeks and they will define the business planning. Also, Jeff will introduce us to the whole team,
19/02 lunch time Andy &amp; Jeff in London
After this conversation, Jeff will share the JD for several the most critica and hard-to-find roles so we can prepare the market research and share the sample profiles + GT Comparison file.', 'VS', '2024-02-01 05:27'),
