  (22762775267::bigint, 10007252162::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, '18/12 CALL NOTES (OLA, VIKA, JOHN, ANDY)

KEY POINTS:
John asked whether we can plan our further work we''ve done for Optegra hospital in Poland on the Business Intelligence. Ola concerned about the deadline: whether we can finish by end of January. John needs to check with Kostia if we manage to finish it in Q1 2024.
New CFO in Poland (Pawel Zaremba came 3 weeks ago) - business owner of the data. If the CFO likes what we''ve done so far, there may be further group level discussions that we can have with him.
New Operations Director (Waldemar Cyrański came 4 months ago in September). Ola needs to catch up with Waldemar and Pawel at the beginning of January to discuss the current roadmap.
Ola is off till 15th of January (3 weeks).
Migration program: majority of services moved to Azure and final 10-20% needs to come out of the data centre. John recalled Segen and migration work we do for them in particular; introduced Artem who can do the planning at a level of detail and understands different data centres that will be helpful. John suggested to introduce Artem to Ola with the idea of helping Optegra with the design piece and then move and lead the execution as needed - Ola agreed it.
Ola: ''''we have a hybrid environment that is running in a red-centric data centre that supports all of our medical devices. The challenge we have is that we don''t have a documentation fully consolidated or a single person, a single person who fully really understands that he''s leaving our business in the UK. We''ve got a little bit of a gap to kind of, you know, understand how the data for all of those medical devices can be shifted. So at the high level, the architecture is not super complex because it''s looking at the file sync and shifting those file shares that are holding the data into the cloud.''''
New head of IT for the UK - Sayad Arzouni - He reports and dots directly to Ola. Ola will introduce him to us. From January, everyone will be reporting to Sayad Arzouni. And then Ops Director''s IT and Marketing have dotted line to Ola.
Another topic to discuss: bring AI into Optegra to solve some of the challenges: Optegra  got a NHS part of the business - the highest volume part of the business. However, the team that supports them, they still do a lot of actually quite manual or on-call interventions. And that''s specifically thinking about how Optegra does preoperative assessments. 1 of the element: Ola said: ''''utilising a voice AI to completely run this full process, being able to essentially, as the patient drops into our referral list, the idea is AI will pick this up.'''' And there was a three day SLA, so it needs to be, have ability to fully dial out, voice, call that patient, do the full voice assessments. I ask all of those questions,
feed the information back to our patient administration system and also book the appointments for that patient. So, you know, there will be specific slots showing off and they should be first, I think it''s two or three strikes. I can''t remember. First available, then the second choice and a third. If they''re not choosing any of those three, then they would go to a different list. So that''s the first part of the process. But then further extending, we want to do all of our clinical calls and so-called follow -up calls with the patient. So after you had the surgery, yes, you come in day one, but actually then one week or three months, you don''t necessarily have to come in. So just call you and ask you several questions. And then fully integrated chat bots. The vision and idea is that you''ve got a fully, almost like a virtual assistant that is managing the full patient journey for both private as well as NHS through the website. So that''s the scope. That''s the element we''re looking at.'''' John said that Artem could be involved there as well.
Ola mentioned that it''d be good to understand the technology landscape, especially for the healthcare element, because at the moment we''ve started essentially in a free of charge POC with a platform called Druid - Romanian company expanding globally very quickly, FDA approved. FDA selected them to utilize for AI across all of the FDA approvals and workflows. And they''ve been running that virtual assistant element for the largest Romanian private hospital, 80% of their transactions is purely done by that. They selected that platform at the moment just only for the POC to essentially prove that the voice and all of those elements can work and they can physically process the patient. So once that''s done, (mid of January), then they will be reviewing and thinking what are the next steps.
Ola mentioned Ufonia - they spending less money there rather than NHS.

NEXT STEPS:
Andy &amp; John to talk to Artem about Druid platform and preferred model of setup,
19/12 Vika to prepare CVs of Sergey and Artem and share them with Ola + summarise our discussion + ask if we can talk early in NY discussion to explore whether we can go..', 'VS', '2023-12-18 08:05'),
