  (22366962387::bigint, 9802469069::bigint, null::bigint, 7667816649::bigint, '05/12 CALL NOTES:

KEY POINTS:
MedPro Systems introduction:
rought on antother vnedor.  Some ups and downs, Started on the main project, the MCR international application Set out to build it had the scope, phase 1 and 2 by the middle of the year Want ed it in place by middle of the year for the conference. Definitely some turnover, interested in what is the normal amount of turnover?
Definitely saw they would bring on a developer then within 3 weeks they were gone, I guess its good that you change rapidly but it creates disruption as well....
The on boarding then needed rework. So we worked hard to get to the august conference, wanted to get to the MVP but we actually just got to a demo, so you can dem ofor an hour but you cant click certain things. What we showed was received very well, some people wanting to buy it right now etc. Looked polished enoughm invested enough in the figma the UX and the wire framing. So we were kind of in a good place, but then from there some weird stuff happened with the vnedor, had some weird falling out with some key people, kind of had a falling out and then morphed into a smaller company, so we are now betting on one small team, it would be analgous to the founders all having a fall out.
So decided to push forward anyway bu things then started to go south, Greg really doubled down on it, brought them in to do another project and 2 other areas where focussing on roadmap.
So this little team now spread across 4 different work streams. At that point really started to question the relationship, getting status reports that are all green. I am a very detailed oriented person, if you tell me its green and I am not sure about it I will go and verify, and look at the code and the underlying database etc etc...
And things being reported as DONE but code been written but not been tested nad not into production its running on laptops etc et.cSO a lot of Medpro folks now getting really converned. Weird place where 2 of these products expected to be in place by January yet nothing in their reporting says they are going to get there.....
So we are expecting an MVP in January and based on Jared assessment they are about 15% done, so there is no way it can be OK.... So the sense is they want to kick the can and then renew and pay more to get more work done....So the project management and the leadership not able to tell us where they are....So, all that being said, Greg is trying to be very optimistic that they are going to catchup and get there, Jared trying to be more realistic and if they dont get there I dont want to keep doubling down, wnat to look at the off ramps and figure out how and where we could do something different....I went htrought the org chart of all the people they brought on, the UX people good, the engineers hard working bu the leadership, teh BAs etc really poor, i could be done tomorrow.....I outline the appraoch to really get the talent righ up front.
PM reports to Jared directly, I want to know whats really slipping, I want the key to the problems, I want the risk registers, I feel like the PMs are managing for them not for us... they are rolling up story points and doing pretty reports...
JH - Do you have anything that is small that we could pick up to“MCR engage”? - its an HCP engagement tool, thats the kind of hting where either we are going to double down and keep going or we are going to say take it over and let someone else run with it. We have the full wire frames and diagrams etc... Some gaps with whats documented in Jira as you have pretty picture but need to have the business rules documented in Jira etc.
TEAM COMPOSITON: A project like that though they brought on a couple of developers and a UX designer. If those developers wanted to leave could they transition?
One good guy in Mexico, he is good I want to keep him, another back end guy also in Mexico... On top of that they reach out to us directly and telL Jared the real story etc...Outlined that potentially vnedor stayig and keeping a couple of ojrects but then working with us on the third one would be good as ithey wold be incsntivised to work with us and trnasition well.....THe other 2 are major roadmap projects to look at rewriting and regenerating large pieces of tech.... I dont think they are doing anything revolutionary, but I am fairly under whelmed by what I am seeing so far, so this may then be a restart and then pass the ball....
NEXT STEPS
Jared has lots internal discussions to do this week, I am pushing to make sure we are starting to look at off ramps, most of our leadership is nervous about what we have.
Jared meets with Greg and Paul again....THe other vendor just seems to have bitten off more than they can chew, the question is can they admit that and then let part of it go as they are struggling,..... I just want transparency, if you take on a project and then you have erally misread it then we should talk about it and renegotiate,
Vika to share our life science deck.
talking to SLT tomorrow and again next week with this being one of the main topics. I would like to start doing a session where I give you the overview and you can start to get an understanding!
to set up another session with Delivery Manager to overview the product etc.', 'VS', '2023-12-05 11:58'),
