  (22164282827::bigint, 9942712775::bigint, null::bigint, 9168847580::bigint, '29/11 CALL NOTES (30-mins)

Intro:
Leah Wilson (joined a call) - Head of Talent, joined in May, 2022
Mark Laws (was optional, didn''t join us) - CTO &amp; Chief Product Officer, as Leah said, but CIO, based on his Linkedin. Previously, John received message from Mark on WhatsApp and mentioned about the current need for hiring. John knows him from GSK for a long period of time.
Kognitiv is a company focused on utilizing data-driven technology to enhance customer loyalty and partnerships. Their mission involves making sense of the data collected by clients to identify valuable opportunities for connecting with customers. They offer technology solutions that simplify the cultivation of loyalty and partnerships, allowing brands to deliver increased value, personalization, and experiences to consumers.
Key notes:
Leah mentioned that in 2020 COVID impacted business a lot. For now, they''re looking for 2-3 Data kings, Data Engineers, someone more Front-end related with good D3 JS skills, ability to code, self-driven, accountable, technology challenges, able to create interactive and dynamic data visualizations. The duration: 3-6 months. Could be full-time basis.
Leah also mentioned that they work with Polish engineers, so would be good to pay attention to this location, initially.
We discussed different models of cooperation and stop on project-based model. Time is crucial, as they want to allocate engineers ASAP, of course, after the notice period.
John’s notes:
Kognitiv operate a SAAS loyalty platform that enables a variety of customers such as credit card companies, retailers, car hire companies, petrol / gas stations to operate their own loyalty scheme where their consumers sign up to collect points and then receive rewards and incentives in the form of discounts, upgrades, gifts etc. The system also contains visual analytics which are designed for clients to understand more about their membership and determine what are the right promotions and campaigns to be won etc, who should be targeted for what offer etc. 
The visualisation aspects are currently all carried out using Tableau, the team we recruit will have responsibility for migrating the system from Tableau as an overlay to an embedded d3.js series of visuals. So we are looking for 3 engineers with the skillsets below that can also have an appreciation of the business goals and be able to carry out the rebuild / migration work. If recruiters need any more insight or background, get them to talk to me first as I worked at Aimia for many years (Aimia subsequently became Kognitiv) so I have a high level understanding of this area and their business that may be useful for us. I would like us to start to look now as if we can find candidates readily available even on a part time basis initially I think we can get a prompt YES decision from Kognitiv, as we heard yesterday, speed is of the essence, so I think in this case, doing some work ahead of the MSA being signed will be a worthwhile gamble.
Next steps:
NDA will be sent from Kognitiv''s side,
MSA (project team) will be sent by GT 29/11 or 30/11 early,
Kognitiv will share the JDs,
GT will prepare the pricing indicatives (hourly rates) + sample profiles.', 'VS', '2023-11-29 11:22'),
