  (20292503023::bigint, 8885526466::bigint, null::bigint, 8432361949::bigint, 'Astellas - 
Exec advisory boards - yes
Works with all the big guys. Japanese pharma so the worst of both worlds, conservative nature of Japanese business and of Big Pharma
THe big players dont challenge that, are typically slow and ponderous and it suits them to be in a slow and ponderous manner!
Long lead times in the life science space though, patience will be a virtue for GT.
Tradtiaional pharma company, strong buy not build model, will rather take a product off the shelf and spend more on it rather than build.
IT not seen as a value add historically, regarded as a bit commodity 
But chagning....
in process of recrutiing a new CTO
and a data analytics function....
Will be more focussed on products...
Wont ever have an army of devleopers in house so players lik GT could be relevant for us in medium and long term.
Data science and machine learning, heavily focussed on Japan even though Pauls role is global
However rapid prorotyping may be of interest, there is a digital innovation team, was originally in Pauls area, but now has become big enough to be worthwhile...
US office is in North Brook, Chicago, Paul will mention and introduce us.... Tom Bower
Also going through an IT reorganiastion, taking more of a product approach with owners of products within each funciton....
May not be so much on the engineering side of things, but will need some help on how to organise from a product side of things....
May well want some advice and guidance from GT on that reorganisation...
There is data science and analytics functions embedded in the business, 
Won''t necessarily hear where the talent gaps are, but Paul will mention us to the head of analytics in tehir business though they may be cutting back more than growing....
Read Albert Ballers book on how Pfizer came up with a covid vaccine.... starting point was we only ahve a certain amount of time.... and it went faster!
Paul challenging to push for 30% saving in time 
Aside - Paul met an adviser at bank of england, pharma 8 years ago was one of the most [productive sectors, now one of the least! So has become slow and inefficeint...
Paul to discuss wtih Tom Bower and will definitely suggest he meets with us', 'JH', '2023-09-19 09:09'),
