  (18928138207::bigint, 8180441284::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, 'Ram front office architect Ramachandran Sivaraman
Transforamtion program, was being driven on a wholesale reorg driven by S4, massively fragmented org, different brands all get hoovered up by different major players
Peroni
Fuller
Asahi
Each of them pretty much operate independently. In the markets where they brew there is such strong brand affinity  of employees and customers that they havent needed to change. But with pressures on margin, this has meant they have to change, they can maintain a level of brand independence but they need to solve their common supply chain challenges.
Built a portal for each of the customers to be able to get an account overview, plan their purchases and make their choices, marketing etc. 
The giants (suoermakrets etc) come through a separate EDI, ie TEscos, Sainsburys etc.
Companies like M&amp;B might use EDI, might go through the portal though as sometimes a bit more localised...
Next phase - a lot of money goes into advertising and promotion, sponsor the Man City group, sponsor the rugby world cup, sponsor Ferrari in the F1, so a lot of money being spent on promotion
But..... they havent been good at building relationship with consumer, they have been going to agencies to buy data and get a list to then sned messages to the consumer
Recent events like Ascot has let them pick up more consumer details and start to build direct B2C loyalty schemes (v simple, ie buy 3 pints, get 1 free). 
But that lets us know more about our consumers and share that with our clients.... 
ie discounts might be better than competitions etc etc. 
Discount hour in Birmingham city centre works well, sticking hte same promoiton in Mayfair probably doesnt...
Will have an app to gather that data....
99% of business today is b2b, by 2030, want to have 20% of sales direct to consumer.
But at the minute no relationship direct to consumer, so starting to build the capabilities of knowledge harvesting of consumer, so in promotion with world cup, Citigroup etc, take that insight from consumer and use that to change relationship with customers and tell them what we know.... 
Might do some redemption in pub but wont really push the app in pubs....
THe idea a few months ago was that they would buy a small chain of pubs and then decide what a digital pub looked like - collect age on phone, manage and measure wastage of beer, how clean are glasses, whats the temperature of hte beer etc etc. 
Could have an order aggregator, forget the guys with EDI as they have done it already, but the medium chains go to Heineken to do the order there, Asahi to do the order there etc etc. No one doing the aggregation across all the brands....
3 parts of it:
Digital bar - no longer want the bricks and mortar, so work with an existing player and do a real pilot around the digital sensors, the ordering etc. 
Consumer engagement and brand affinity - could be an app, could be product websites etc
Order aggregator that helps teh B2B players.... Would like to white label it and not necessarily associate it with Asahi so that non Asahi customers might use it so we can collect even more data....
Suggested Andrew Muzelle as an introduction, the outside in view on loyalty could be hugely valuable, particularly the Sainsburys background etc... 
Ethan - wants to treat this as a product development, not a traditional corporate requirements approach....
digital bar and order aggregator - could treat that as a more traditional engagement for GT with the right capabilities in place under Asahi leadership
For the consumer piece - then potentially Andrew, Justin and Andy could then have an innovation workshop that allowed them to understand what the target looks like, the ideation part massively important but we need the soup to nuts approach with product capability 
andy asked the question on how creative you would be, for example, if there was a proposal for a dating app that allowed to book bars, buy beer, etc but have a dating app as the core, would that kind of creative thinking be accpeted?
So Adam who owns this transformation very creative, bu moves to new ideas quite quick - 6 months ago wanted to focus on Metaverse, has now aligned to the three goals Ethan outlines.... 
Asahi Europe - really runs as a self contained subsidiary, presents financial data back to Japan but nothing more than that. 
Andy - rising star in the app world called OneZone - that is a sort of experience version of OpenTable, gives you very contextualised experience based categories rather than jsut books a table, ie "this is hottest new restaurant in Mayfair, with a DJ", so dining category is dining with DJ... So they are interesting they have aggregated, it falls through your hand with a beautiful architecture, could even be something Asahi could buy.... Remember in b2C you need to look not so much as where the demographic is today but where they want to be.....
Suggested that we do a proposal to build the more basic capabilities - digital pub and ability to buiild the aggregator...
Wouldnt want to do this with big guys, BUT the problem is that the organisation will instinctively think about the 
Adam - the budget relates to marketing, he is really innovative, he watns to do something different, he has got his rugby world cup budget and formula one budget, and next year he will have City group budget, this is probably the area to focus on, he is most excited by the direct to consumer piece.... 
So meet with Adam, give him a freebie, then do something for 20k ish to then give him the animations and ideas that get him to the point where he is itching to build it.
So a couple of hours in their office in Woking..... 
John to send over a brief overview of what the ideation session looks like, introduce Justin and Andrew, workshop session for a couple of hours in Woking, get their marketing guy excited, then lead to 20k engagement for product design / animation etc...
Then hopefully build it all out!!', 'JH', '2023-07-17 08:47'),
  (18928521418::bigint, 8288072675::bigint, 27401::bigint, null::bigint, 'Knows Maureen Wedderburn - doesnt really like her! 
Stories about Andrew Witty... fixed his PC in the old days
Then PA consulting, 
Malcolm 
Came in 2 years ago to MRN, the MRN has been around for 17 years, focusses on decentralised clinical trials but not really on the technology, going to be offering a lot more technoilogy going forward becasue we have to but the core service offering is providing health care professionals either at the site or the patients home...... 
If you are an alzheimer patient going to a site to take medicine and report is a nightmare and if you have a Red condition even more so. 
So we send nurses into folks homes to administer trail medicine, and take vital signs, globally
Based in milton keynes and in Chicago
Use some nurses on payroll, some on zero hours contracts, sisue them laptops / ipads etc...
Pandemic saw them collapse from 80 people initially but then grew to 360 people as big pharma wanted them to do studies in peoples homes....
But last year Roche pulled an Alzheimers compound that took 7 million out of revenue.
So focus now is to build up the pipeline for this year and for next year, looking at efficiency, trying to get rid of the defcicity, a lot of overworked peopel, want folks working smarter not as many hours, looking at not replacing people they lose.... 
That said, market is warming up again, investors havnet invested in biotechs as much so less business from them
A lot of the competition came from big CRO''s who had bought up competitirs so now one of the only players that can do the in home medicine and trials, there are some others as well....
Couple of business units they are setting up, technologies business unit where they are investing in e source data captire software, telemedicine, e consent allt he things people ask about when they are lookign at decentralsied clin trials. 
Also looking at which CRO services could offer in congjuntion with the HCP model they have got, what could they do to help sites perform better wiether through patient recruitment or professional support, probably not a huge UK model as a lto of situes in UK are NHS, but there are places around Europe where sites focus just on research..... 
telemedecine - struggled with it as we are not famous for doing technology...
A lot of the services we offer are pass through serviecs from a vendor
video conferencing that has to be secure, zoom for medicine etc.
Patient reported outcomes
devices etc. 
Potential touch points with the patient, we effectively get paid for, so the more touch points with the patient the more we get paid for the study, so if we can collect more data on behalf of the sponsor we get paid for that.... 
Often we sign a sponsor for 10m but only see 5m over hte life of th study as not enough patients signed up, not enoug hhomeo visits etc etc. 
Story - went to see Professor Harden talk, the vice leader of the vaccine program, did a talk in Malcolms village, caught covid from number 10, he talked about Matt Hancock, all agreed that he is an idiot.... 🙂 
Described our medical support desk - he got very excited, teh help desk that they run tody has about 10% of IT queiries, but als has 80-90 % of process querieis on how to do it.
They have built this service for themselves BUT would like to sell it on to their customers and for folks looking for support across the CRO world.
Would we help build this? 
Runs business quality development, its a family owned business, family are all employed in the business, 2 parents and the kids. Until quite recentlky had all 3 kids reporitng into him, one of them now is off to run the technology business. All smart kids, not nepotisum
Malcolm looks after continuous improvement, learning and development, IT INfrasturtcure, etc everyghing non billable other than finance and HR. Also has a responsibility for R&amp;D. Guy that we need to talk to abou tthis is ALex Wiley, he is going off to run the technology stuff, he was looking at this last year, then the ROche thing happened. 
Could introduce us to the head of IT as well that reports into him. Go into Milton Keynes and meet with them all. So if there are things that wont cost a lot but can deliver value they will do it, BUT they will also be planning budget cycle for next year..... 
Does also need to look at all the advanced analytics stuff. Everything they have runs in Salesforce today, how they manage visits to commercial development to quality management, all runs in Salesforce and it works. Just lost entire business intelligence team, so aware of those gaps and what else we could do...
Shared the fact we had won BI at Optegra as well, pitched as they had lost their BI team and asked us to fix the reports and then maintain etc.... 
Nikita outlined our partnership approach, Malcolm very clear that he does not want a bodyshopping model, he outlined he had 12 people in BI once lost them all, no one screaming at him looking for 
Invite to HOC..... 
Send invite. WIll also try and get his CEO 
Is a rugby fan, wnet to parliamentary awards for rugby... 
Malcolm - rugby, cycling, has lost 3 stone in last 19 weeks.... 
Not a huge footy fan, likes the womens game, want to 6 nations for ladies rugby,', 'JH', '2023-07-17 08:47'),
