  (17740609257::bigint, 7545096912::bigint, null::bigint, 7667887330::bigint, 'Frankie Call Notes :

Introduced to Phil CTO via the CEO Phil Lawson. He said their business is primarily touch screen sign in solutions. Primarily education branching out into commercial. they do all the software and Hardware installation services.
Current situation – number of installs in UK 5500. All on premise solution. Creating scalability issues. Need to move to the cloud. All dev done in house in Leeds.Not got enough devs – 8-10+ couple of contractors. Going to take a couple of years to move into the cloud long term. Going to have to continue to develop the product for BAU / updates / functionality –as they move into  commercial sector – new demands – multi tenanted offices/ contractor sign in. their current version they refer to as Version 4 - ./net stack – Microsoft sequel database. Data provides resting api. Touch screen application – winforms. Winforms application back end. Gut feeling is that we will zammerim application on the local system with an asp web front end.Integrations at the moment a lot – 13 diff management systems. Ideal scenario – remote teams – one of our developers as part of that team-4 remote teams 4 dev one on each team.  He likes the extended team model concept. Ideal start date ASAP. Project funded by current business sold and pipeline.  He is going to send through the job descriptions for me to send to the team to confirm in our sweet spot and also the prices.

Nick Call Notes:

2 of them started the business 8 years back (both called Phil)! Phil Brooke wrote the original product, other Phil is the Business guy.
5,500 installations now, and they are great at Sales, market leader in UK (only 30 are non-UK).

One of the major benefits of moving to the Cloud is that currently, they struggle to find Engineers to do the installations because they need to do the physical installation AND the technical configuration on-site. if they were in the Cloud, they could on-board Engineers much more easily as they would only need to do the Physical installation.  

Reason Phil thinks it could take as long as 2 years is that it will involved a complete Re-Write of the product / a move to Micro Architecture.  Currently it is a SQL on-premise model, no tenants.  It is a WINFORMS applocation, and they will need a web interface (think they will  need ZAMERIN in the future.
https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/xamarin/
Pitched embracent Expertise / Programme Leadership / DevHub heavy lifting as an option to build on Frankie''s call and he is open to a call with paul mason -- and a meeting.  THinks that if they go with Offshore Teams, they would want one Dev in the UK hub to work closely and be able to ensure the learning remains with the Business long-term (an approach that would work nicely with the DevHub model).

Will arrange for a call with Paul Mason.  


Paul Mason- Meeting Notes:

Hi, the meeting was good. Myself and Dave Sanderson from Inciper attended as Gary needed to be in London. We met with Phil Brooke and the new Development Manager, Paul. The focus on the session was understanding what they were trying to achieve and their current proposed architecture. They require help to validate this approach. An example is the database on which to build the solution – SQL or MongoDb. There is little documentation at this point.

The new Dev Manager was initially quite defensive as we tried to understand the current approach but it is clear that Phil wants an additional view point and the proposal that I am considering is a paid engagement of a 3 day workshop and the delivery of a Solution Blueprint to go through the various architectural components and validate or propose alternative approaches.

This is not in my skillset to deliver but Dave was comfortable that he could do it. We spent 2 hours going through the current and planned requirements so have a good insight and understand the challenges that they are trying to address.

In terms of delivery, Phil is looking to Paul to be the development lead and to deliver the solution with supplementary high quality resources to extend his team to complete the build. This does align to the DevHub model rather than pass the delivery to a third-party. He wants to align the current resources with these high quality resources so that they are upskilled to move into BAU.

Both Dave and I commented after the meeting is that the risk for InVentry is that Paul did not appear to have the experience to deliver this solution and this is why Phil is keen to talk to us.

I am awaiting feedback from Dave and will go back to Phil early next week for the Solution Blueprint proposal.
If you want more info let me know.', 'MK', '2020-08-06 08:28'),
