  (17740797376::bigint, 7545055475::bigint, 4990::bigint, 7667570373::bigint, 'Chrisitian is only responding via LinkedIn these days.&nbsp; Email is completely unresponsive.', 'AB', '2021-03-01 07:37'),
  (17739077310::bigint, 7544896964::bigint, 5503::bigint, 9141496260::bigint, 'Pre-conditions you need to know about Stepler:
Cross-platform (ReactNative) step-tracking mobile app. Track steps, watch ads -&gt; get Stepler coins -&gt; buy real goods with those coins.Originally launched in Sweden, later launched in Norway too.Team of owners originally consisted of 4 persons - Daniel (owner, decision maker, Stepler was not his main job until now), Niklas (CEO, tier2 decision maker, mostly busy with marketing), Emil (CTO, his main job got funding recently so he''d like to leave Stepler soon), Semir (dunno what he''s doing, not a decision maker).Besides 2mc they had a company doing some devOps things part-time - IT Svit.They had 2mc providing 2 developers on a project basis, each for $40 per hr. Besides getting 2 developers they had a PM and QA specialists as a bonus, for free. Though QA services were not ideal. They don''t expect anything for free from this cooperation though and QA is not a pain point, just a note.From the very beginning of cooperation with 2mc they were curious to build own team in Ukraine.They love to hang out and close deals by meeting the partner in personal.So I had a call with Daniel this morning discussing his expectations. Here''s what we''ve got:
They''d like to start with 1 senior fullstack who will later turn into a Product Manager / CTO. This guy should be able to make product solutions, manage and be a major part of following team hiring process, get all the knowledges from Emil, review 2mc and IT-Svit during the transition process and review the code and tech solutions of an upcoming team. They expect that this guy may stop coding with the flow of time, e.g. as soon as the team''s formed.They don''t think that''s reasonable to break with 2mc as soon as the first ET person is landed. They expect it to be a smooth transition process while we''re hiring new people.They prefer keeping IT-Svit as a part-time devOps assistants. They expect us to find them a part-time UI/UX designer aswell (1 week per mo. workload expected).They don''t know how to do best for a QA - hire a fulltime QA or do smth. similar to the IT-Svit schema.Their expectations are to hire 5 persons till this summer.They''d love @Vlad to be involved into all the processes as their account manager, maybe as a partial project manager at the very beginning of team setupThey have some other companies to consider besides GT, though I''d say we''ve got chances to get a deal.Why do they want to make ET instead of project workload they''ve got from 2mc right now?
cause Daniel finally started working on Stepler fulltime and he finds himself ready to manage the Stepler way better than beforecause they believe that this is a better option to grow faster and be more responsive to the market needscan''t say they got negative experience from 2mc workers but time to time team setup was changing because of several reasons', 'MK', '2021-02-19 07:51'),
