  (17738800627::bigint, null::bigint, 3832::bigint, 7667887062::bigint, 'Sits in major R&amp;D site, Maidenhead,
Potential intro for Eagle Genomics with Syngenta, Paul taking a look and will check if any other collaborations already ongoing.... May well be interested in intro
Paul - looks across all IT and digital, sourcing and supplier management, more efforts and energies go into operating model, really internal advisers to IT. Had been so heavily outsourced that they hurt themselves, had outsourced all their business analysts and architecture to Infosys...Paul came in 5 years ago, monolithic relationships in tower, 100m dollar relationships in each tower, huge spend, outsourced to the point where people turning up with the 90 slide presentation to justify the dashboard was green even if it didn''t feel that way....Changed under last CIO, deliberately went best of breed and cloud to try and break apart these monolithic relationships etc.... And a lot of what time was spent doing was dismantling while focussing on getting the A team....Digital - the businesses went out and formed their own digital strategies versus one Basle based central approach.
Then new CIO took back the digital agenda from Deloitte, took the strands back where people had done loyalty and other pieces, pulled them into platforms, then allow a localization on top of that.Now gone down a more augment route.Now having a think about some longer term relationships and keen to find the right kind of team to work close with them.
On the IT side of things, bigger design side of things, trying to work out where people have gone down certain routes.... Salesforce, an example, became in-sourced and augmented, as a maturity would like to reshape and do that in a different way.And other black box things where R&amp;D might have some competitive capability yet its completely outsourced...So also keen to have some capability geographic
R&amp;D have used EPAM, had some good engineers out of Ukraine but have possibly over used them for some of the wrong things etc....
Can potenitally be a mis match where a good partner gets overpaid for the wrong things...
Team trying to come up with the right models and supplier and almost have a bit
I outlined how we would want to work with enterprises, let us get involved with building and shaping the real challenges, not just filling in RFP''s etc.But can we really outline how we would solve your probelm rather than ticking boxes....
Could potentially use more in digital or IT....So internally, working with engineering, launched a disparate set of products and acquisitions, 125million hectares of land under our digital programs of any of the competition... Done it through augmentation primarily in India, but now there is thought that need some intimacy and interaction in the region. I the Ukraine have a company acquired called Cropio, relatively small farm management company aiming to integrated and grow from there, but therefore a possible opportunity to grow from there.....
Definitely sounds like there could be a space there and some interest in the future....
Give Paul a couple of weeks to shape and work on the demand and so on, looking for openness to switch from augmentation to some more focussed teams
Meet again in 2 - 3 weeks time, introduce Andy, send some background in the meantime, could be really exciting for R&amp;D and Digital in future', 'JH', '2021-03-04 03:59'),
