  (17740753873::bigint, 7545055456::bigint, 5308::bigint, 7667859938::bigint, 'SHORT SUMMARY ABOUT THE COMPANY (PRODUCT) 
Avocet is a demand side platform, advertising trading platform for brands, businesses, anyone who wants to buy advertising on the internet, a system designed to connect to advertising exchanges, place bids, deliver creatives, provide the workflows around that etc. Its a pretty big platform given the resources they have had over the year, spending 50k USD on AWS, handling 100 billion HTTP requests a month, that is an established business. 

They want to do some improvements but there is also a new set of products they would like to build. The new focus is a different area of digital advertising that is the measurement of creative delivery, its attention, how it interacts with the user etc. It’s called an attention measurement platform
 
They currently have a team of 4 developers including CTO Simon who is leaving the team after he makes hires. They need an additional team of 3 ETMs
 
How did they hear about GT?
Simon Critchley - CTO and founder of Avocet knows John Harris through Decentralized Advertising business and heard about our services to build extended teams. 
 
Experience in managing remote teams
Yes partially.
 
Do they have a clear understanding of their needs?
Yes. They want to do some improvements but there is also a new set of products they would like to build. The new focus is a different area of digital advertising that is the measurement of creative delivery, its attention, how it interacts with the user etc. It’s called an attention measurement platform
 
Technical Savvyness
Advanced
 
Financial Resilience
Well funded but pre-revenue.  Expect to be revenue positive by EoY
 
Team Requirements
1 x Senior Site Reliability Engineer (Go)
Core role would fit under site reliability engineering role, SRE, building platform and maintaining platform services, back end and full stack engineers with a focus on GOLANG. Platform is fully written in GO, running in Kubernetes, it’s a hybrid of feature development, no dedicated dev ops, so it’s handled across the team. They want engineers who can write the code and manage the end to end deployment.
1 x Junior Site Reliability Engineer (Go)
1 x Senior Frontend Engineer 
Currently they have one engineer with react and angular, so having a back up there would be good.
 
Existing HR Processes
Not existentt, would need GT’s help in career growth opportunities for developers
 
Other Remote Workers
Team has gone fully remote since the Covid-19. 
 
Is GT the sole partner
Yes
 
Established Engineering Team
Partially. At the minute, they have Simon and one other engineer in place on the Front end. They had another engineer at the back end who has gone on a sabbatical, but its’ far from guaranteed that they will come back.
 
Roadmap Defined:   TBC
 
Final Decision Maker:  CTO &amp; CEO', 'MK', '2021-05-05 04:25'),
  (17738800611::bigint, null::bigint, 3830::bigint, null::bigint, 'Speculative Introduction via my brother.
Gulliver lives in Ibiza, Masters in artificial intelligence from Edinburghmoved into media, been doing media tech for 20 years, used to write code, now develops large scale streaming platform productsWas global head of product for the BBCThen went to Sony, was CTO for direct to consumer for Sony on the entertainment, whats on TV now, etc...Sony had team of about 250, then moved away from digital so took redundancy
CTO now of small company in LA, running them at night from Ibiza,They do accelerator services for small companies, tidy them up, get them board members, sort out their funding problems, help with with research etcReal estate tokenisation business, trying to sell millennials £2 of a hotel et.c.Then got another one which is like a programmable internet, so its networks as code, to route networks intelligently, then use AI to learn those routes, so you can get your traffic optimised,
Generally tech businesses, led by tech...Also, sort out supply chains, they came into contracts, looked to sort out supply chains and reduce working capital, saved 5million for Sony, gave them 1million, Saved CBS 20 million 
Anything where there is a big amount of infrastructure, databases, CDNs etc.... Never seen them not get at least 20% off a CDN bill. so you have bought  acceleration which isn''t needed etc.... Made enough money last year that they decided they didn''t want to do the same thing quite the same way, so now cleaning up supply chains to be carbon neutral, now doing same thing, trying to be efficient, forensically analysing logs to ensure that service levels hit etc. But now focussing a bit more on sustainability etc...
Great roster of clients, president and CTO is a guy named Tony, lived next door to Steve JObs in Aspen, has an  amazing address book etc... Tony is really the engine with the network from heaven as it were...
Uses Crowdbotics at the minute, will do you an app for 20k, its not proper tech but its great for rapid prototyping...
Data science - was interested if GT could help if he needed a data science platform to be captured with the right instrumentation,
Also mentioned they do a lot of Wellness stuffThrive marketplace, founder is someone they know well, they in accelerator smart have 50%, selling supplements direct to consumers, particularly in the US, so they go off and look at plant samples and botany...They want to build a tech platform that sits under all thrive records, where you go in and record your symptoms, potentially there might be some overlap with my skills and background...
Ukraine - looking to build a data platform for the real estate company, might look at some of that stuff for himOn the wellness side could be some things of interestAPple captures hard stuff, doesn''t capture how well you are feeling etc... your watch isn''t going to tell you that, looking at dashboards that become a bit more subjective,Need to give some thought with the schemas on what folks are interested in, how might you develop direct to consumer versions on the back of that etc. Also involved with Ketamine clinics for PTSD etc..', 'JH', '2021-01-05 13:25'),
