  (17740679112::bigint, null::bigint, 5506::bigint, 7667570377::bigint, 'Helicon health - is a company started life, delivering stroke prevention, david patterson founder professor of cardiovascularDeveloped Open EHR open health record and interoperability standard, registered with ISO\Needed to bring a product to market to use the standardrecognised there was a need between shared care between GPs, patients and hospitals. So healthy heart helped manage the warfarin interaction between them, algorithm to help them keep in the therapeutic reange
Now adding app and elearning, health care professionals can get elearning on line etc.Never really got the growth, it sustained, but never really grew. 2 other players one in primary, one in acute who did well
and pharma companies introduced NOAX which is replacing Warfarin, so healthcare trusts don''t usually buy in spaces where medicine going down
But won a clin trial for NHS, so use of apps and wearable such as fitbit so being used to measure whether interventions could be made earlier, to see whether
million pound trial, Helicon 500k, wrote the bid, needed Phillips alongside them for their tech and for balance sheet
TOny led bid and trial from agile, and David from medical perspective.
What happened is that they signed a contract, closed consulting, then brought In Touch health, now part of Teladoc, 36billion company. We are now distributor for their company in UK, that put revenue back in our pockets at time when product going back into furloughSold a really good product to Alder Hey specialist consultants to do remove medicine between hospitals in liverpool and alder Hey for babies and maternity care. Growing fast, won an award for thatProfile has risen with the knowledge transfer networkClose loop medicine products, drug, device and data involved, so where you can personalise and use the device to collect sensor data, personalise dosage, very similar to what they do within stroke prevention for warfarin.New one in stroke which detects atrial fibrillation, needs to go through clin trial, get the right approvals etc.Have another one where device is invented but not developed yet, needs money to be built and go through clin trial - stomach motility, measures the speed at which stomach empties, sensor on stomach and back, particularly good for babies and thinner people, used instead of putting a radioactive isotope in someone''s stomach (sintigrophy)....Another product for prostate cancer, enabling men to self care and manage condition without going to hospital all the time, give them data about their condition so they could manage themselves.I am hopeless at development - i have one smart guy, one who is great at maintaining code but very hard to communicate with .... But I think we need more development capability and more capability overall... along the lines you were describing....
Java - open source database, postgres Sql, has an awful lot of stored procedures, needs updating a lot of the procedures are out of date... Possibly need to rehost that app at some stage....
Some of the projects are start ups, some are a bit further on... Shall we try and find one project to get started on, could well be picking up the engineering of course
Rather than do it all now, why don''t I have a chat with David Patterson, then see how we could lay out the principle elements, dont want to frighten david moygan (existing developer) to death....', 'JH', '2020-11-24 07:53'),
