  (17738799815::bigint, 7544855785::bigint, 3906::bigint, 7667816643::bigint, 'Vodori - introduced via a third party recruiter so we may need to work out a referral bonus if this goes further. Scott Rovegno is CEO, Grant Gochnauer is CTO, both founders. Scott Rovegno , Grant Gochnauer -amplifying our own research into Ukraine,A thinking engineer is alway sbetter than a robotic engineer.Grant - CTO and one of founders with Scott, v technical, computer science bacgkround, products, codiginf fevelope,ent, leading engineering teams, mostly back end focussed so everything from database, infra, back end development, less of a frong end person. Pretty familiar over past 3 or 4 years built this cloud product, learned a lot about building multi tenant SAAS, lots of opportunity to continue scaling, enhancing and replatofrming what we hae built so farScott - one of founders, was once tecnical, datawarejoise and BI, grew up implementing Documentum, back in 2005 when founded Vodori saw some of the pattenrs, commercial open source, virtualisation.Now deedicated life sciences exepcte dto be so for the forseeable future.built a number of customised app ,each customer got an app and we customised it for tehm. Then 2016 Zinc ahead got scooped up by Veeva, customers were grouchy, they liked the fact 2 folks bid on their product, so when Zinc went away, all of this knowledge gave the means and need to fall into vacancy when Zinc got scooped up, gel we could take on Veeva in the meerging and mthe middle markets and at the minimum they were hungfry for a competitive bid.... The thesis that there is unmet need has been proven true and now in agressive scaling mode, scaling up, cpaacity to do more, quarter over quarter based on makret demand. Launched 2 new products last year, analytics and sales enablement platofrm pepper folio, been talking to folsk in past couple of months about companies that do what we do.they are not looking for staff augmentation, want people on our Slack, act as though they are Vodori employees not just the hired help.
The Veeva comparison and their lack of creativity and price resonated.
Vodori is a direct competitor with Promomats....
At a high level, then potentially we could do an NDA, then some slides that spell out current situation through the end of this year potentially as a pilot fo rthe collaboration
Pepper folio - very much more about features than scaling and platform a good candidate to be outsourced or collaboratively devleoped with an outsourced paertner, would be great to work together, we really dont wnat order takers, we are lookgin for folks who have been around mult tenant b2b saas, folks who have built consumer clouds millions and millions of users thats fine, bu the b2b AWS expeirence is really valuable to us so finding the right kind of folks that can assist in technical design, architects, tech lead profiles etc.Folio lends itself to a quarter long pilot, potneenitally collaboration on an integrated development model that could then start to assist on Pepper flow...
Looking for a success based expansion, it would be a 25% capacity initially, but iover time it would be the majority of the team, so the goal would be prove it, optimise it and scale it....Folio is not a one and done, its a multi year roadmap so on the assumption that experiemnet works, but conceptually there is a body of work around folio, concepts are similar but not corolloray to Ppepper flow, bu ideally we would then bring engineers on board, train them, on board them etc...So this is something that can evolve and grow.Potential for 4-6  squad, team composition can be eveolved as we go but certainly engineering, some srot of tech leadership, they already have a really talented QA that is in place in their organsiation, then as the team size gets higher then there can be a team growth2 different teams have slightly different responsiblities, tech stack is Angular version 11 (modern vesion) then a combination of java Closure on the back end htough moving away from Closure to pure Java.Then there is the platform team providing platform as a product with multi tenancy API product, some devops capabilities, the tech stack there is Java, a little bit of Closa thsi si the core AWS, multi tenancy design stack experites and the apps kind of sit on top.... So almost indepdenent of each other....
Also needs to have the ability to do releases, software validation, they could do this on their own, but really want to use partners if tehy could, have also partnered with Amazon to get expertise etc...
Next step, NDA, send us deck, talk through highlights, give us reaction to fit within our team and model, budget and quote. Though budget nto such an issue, the other 2 companies he is talking to are in agreement that the talent and hunger is there, the partnership and team structure is there, but the part that intrigues him most is the ability to tap into me and others who have life sciences experts, we don need nor expect to have unicorns with life sisence expertise and engineerrs, but how can then ebnefit from osmosis through our other life sicence clients and teams, tahts a significaint differentiator for them.The timing is the other thing...  are wer looking 4, 6, 8 or 12 weeks to get stood up?US market is currently mad....However if you told me 16 weeks but the team is brilliant that would be OK
Tech team is scattered in US, hired in Idaho, so combination of folks wanting to be in other places, its more remote than previously but the ability to be productive including timezones with Kiev is a something we are confident with but how we build culture is slightly unknown, its important to us but
I indiciated 8-12 weeks in the current climate and the life sciences space
Shared possibility of intro to Emma Hyland - looking at 18-24 months expansion as they get series A funding etc but could be a good intro now...
Send out NDA, review deck, make quote, intro anduy', 'JH', '2021-05-19 07:36'),
  (17740796604::bigint, null::bigint, 4712::bigint, 7667791343::bigint, 'IONOS is a leading provider of cloud infrastructure, cloud services, and hosting with more than eight million customer contracts. The product portfolio offers everything that companies need to be successful in the cloud: from domains to classic websites and do-it-yourself solutions, from online marketing tools to full-fledged servers and IaaS solutions. The portfolio is aimed at freelancers, small businesses, and consumers as well as enterprise customers with complex IT requirements. IONOS was created in 2018 from the merger of 1&amp;1 and IaaS provider ProfitBricks. IONOS is part of the listed United Internet AG (ISIN DE0005089031). The IONOS brand family includes STRATO, Arsys, Fasthosts, home.pl, InterNetX, SEDO, United Domains and World4You.', 'MK', '2021-05-25 07:20'),
