  (17740796117::bigint, 7545019096::bigint, 4104::bigint, 7667569905::bigint, 'How did they hear about GT? 
Previous GT client: Asitha Rodrigo who was formerly Reevoo''s CTO
Service Type:  Extended Team

Decision Maker:  Asitha Rodrigo (CTO)
Hiring Manager:  Balaji Jayavelu (VP of Eng in Bangalore)
What does their product do?Mobile ''on demand'' payment for medical insurance and medical care.  A subscription model that is based on cash availability on each day of a subscription month.  If you can only afford 20 days, you pay only for 20 days coverage.
Product MaturityPayment platform Stack is currently in BETA until end July.  Want to build a robust scalable production architecture before EoY.
Roadmap DetailsTBD
Existing TeamHeavily reliant on team of 60 engineers in Bangalore, with further product teams in Singapore and UK.  They also use outsource agencies in Sri Lanka

Are they sufficiently funded?Yes.  They are revenue positive and trading in over 14 countries in Asia and Asia Pac but they are also starting a new investment round in July/August 2021 to help them scale faster across Asia.
Current pain points? 
Heavily reliant on team of 60 engineers in Bangalore, with further product teams in Singapore and UK.  They are unable to scale fast enough and have current blockages in building a robust payment platform with API capabilities.  Although peer to peer transactions are used widely, digital payment technology for recurring services is still in its infancy across India and most of Asia.  Simply isn''t enough credit in mobile payment accounts to accommodate ongoing subscriptions.  THis is a huge obstacle for BIMA who hopes to introduce a fully functional and easy to use, low cost payment and credit system for health insurance and later on medical care.

Requirements (Team size, skills mix,  PT/Ext Team/DS, Immediate &amp; long term requirements)?
TBD
Urgency, Timeline for onboarding (earliest/latest, or known date)?
Q3
Tech Stack?
BE: Java with preferences for Springboot, Reddit, Cache, Netflix OS, Springcloud, Mongo DBFE: Google Flutter &amp; DartAWS Cloud

Has Existing HR onboarding processes and policies (list any specific requirements around testing, data protection, background checks etc)?
TBD
Other Notes', 'AB', '2021-06-18 06:48'),
  (17740608232::bigint, null::bigint, 4170::bigint, null::bigint, 'Jigsaw - variety of businesses, tech and media focussed, including an Apple focussed reseller and systems integrator to small businesses etc.
Jason heads the M&amp;E business focussing on the media industry, in particular the post production side of things. 40 or 50 post houses round the UK but mainly focussed London and Salford, huge money involved, typically filming happens in summer, a lot of the post production work and editing happens in spikes during winter, though that is changing.
Huge cloud uptake from their clients, primarily AWS, some Azure, not much google other than niche in Latin America.Jason sstrategy is building out their own capability with Nutanix, then leveraging the public cloud to burst accordingly.For the post houses and some of the major TV companies being able to provide an end to end service is key, also an outsource model where they can stand up engineering capability to take on client projects.Dev Ops is a critical area for them, potential to build out a small extended team which Jason then sells on to his clients.... v exciting work, some big brand names in their client list, IMG, UKTV, ITN, others etc.He has a v expensive contract engineer that leads a lot of their build out in this space, it could be he could lead the team and then have some Ukraine resources working for him.Also interested in our ability to burst and provide project based capability to support as needed.
Suggested looking at media as a sector anyway, the AWS space in particular is huge, the volumes are colossal.Could be worth an indicative quote, send him over the kind of media focussed DevOps people we could find, I told him it was 12k USD for a top devops person, he didnt blink, understood its about talent rather than labour arbitrage.Nothing this year, but could come to life early in new year, will keep talking.', 'JH', '2021-11-10 08:10'),
  (17740397293::bigint, 7545019099::bigint, 5306::bigint, 7667887347::bigint, 'How did they hear about GT? 
Through Reevoo (Lisa Ashworth).  Feefo acquired Reevoo in August 2021.  Brief Description of Product/ServiceCustomer Reviews and online targeting optimisation platform for B2B, specialising in Retail, Property, Financing, Automotive sectors among others.https://www.feefo.com/

Are they sufficiently funded?Yes, already revenue positive at £25M recurring annual revenue with additional venture-backed funding (unspecified) and an existing employee base of approx 150.
