  (17425167584::bigint, null::bigint, null::bigint, 7457036009::bigint, 'GT''s understanding of the current business challenges
Latest News
LinkedIn News Feed
In general, they post about cancer and how their platform helps to detect it early. Nothing special on the tech side, but interesting in regard to their new launches and types of cancer they can detect.

What do they do?
Ezra AI is a New York-based healthcare company that specializes in using artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) to improve early cancer detection. The company offers a full-body MRI scan that uses AI technology to analyze images for potential signs of cancer or other abnormalities. The scan is non-invasive and does not involve any radiation exposure, making it a safer alternative to other imaging tests like CT scans or X-rays.
Ezra AI''s scan is designed to detect early signs of various types of cancer, including prostate, breast, ovarian, pancreatic, and liver cancers, among others. The company''s AI algorithms analyze the MRI images and flag any areas that may require further attention or follow-up testing. If the scan detects any abnormalities, the patient is referred to a board-certified radiologist for further evaluation and diagnosis.
In addition to its cancer screening services, Ezra AI also provides patients with access to genetic counseling and testing, as well as personalized recommendations for lifestyle changes and preventive measures to reduce their risk of developing cancer.

Financial and business performance information:
Ezra AI had raised over $40 million in funding from investors. Some of their major investors include GV (formerly Google Ventures), Accomplice, Founders Future, and Credo Ventures.
In October 2020, Ezra AI raised $18 million in a Series A funding round led by Accomplice, with participation from GV and other investors. The company stated that the funds would be used to expand its services to new regions, enhance its AI technology, and support research and development efforts.
In addition to external funding, Ezra AI has also received grants and partnerships from various organizations, including the National Institutes of Health and the Prostate Cancer Foundation, to support its research and development initiatives.


Open positions / Hiring strategy/trends
Currently no open positions in IT. In general, their headcount of engineering + IT + QA is only 13 people. Had 2 IT role openings more than 6 months ago.




What network connections do we have to have a chat and get more intelligence?
Full list of CXOs and Director+ personas in Linkedin. Need the help of John H to check for 2nd-degree connections to any of these people.

GT Approach
Their CCO, Jason Goodman, had lunch with Andy and John in London. They are interested in Intro to Eagle doing a coaching session for them. Also, looking to discuss their engineering needs for the UK product launch in Q4. They agreed to meet with their CEO, Emi Gal, in London in mid-June.

What conferences do they speak at or attend?
Looks like they do not focus their marketing and sales efforts on conferences. Haven''t seen any posts on Ezra or CEO''s / CCO''s news feeds. The product is mainly a B2C offering.  

Do they have any external contractors as with GT?
The engineering team looks decent for a startup. Looks like outsourcing is minimized or absent completely. Need further exploration with Ezra''s stakeholders.', 'VO', '2023-05-06 12:43'),
