Benevolent AI is a UK-based technology company that uses artificial intelligence to discover and develop new drugs. It was founded in 2013 and has raised significant funding since its inception. As of September 2021, the company had raised a total of $292 million in funding, according to Crunchbase. Some of the company''s notable investors include Woodford Investment Management, Lansdowne Partners, and Temasek, as well as strategic partnerships with major pharmaceutical companies such as AstraZeneca
AstraZeneca and Novartis. In 2019, Benevolent AI raised $90 million in a funding round led by Temasek, which valued the company at over $2 billion.

