What do Exscientia.Ai do?
Exscientia.ai is a leading company in the field of artificial intelligence (AI) drug discovery, focusing on using AI to accelerate the discovery and development of new drugs. The company was founded in 2012 and has since grown into one of the world''s leading AI-based drug discovery companies, with offices in the UK, US, and Japan.
Exscientia.ai has developed a proprietary platform called Centaur Chemist, which uses AI and machine learning algorithms to rapidly design and optimize new drug compounds. The platform is able to analyze vast amounts of data and identify potential drug targets and compounds in a fraction of the time it would take traditional drug discovery methods.
Exscientia.ai has collaborations with leading pharmaceutical companies and has already generated several pre-clinical and clinical candidates. Their AI-driven drug discovery approach has shown promising results, with faster discovery times and improved success rates in identifying potential drug candidates.

Financial and business performance information:
Exscientia.ai has raised significant funding from investors, including the Japanese pharmaceutical company Sumitomo Dainippon Pharma, which invested $90 million in the company in 2019. The company has also entered into partnerships with several pharmaceutical companies, including Sanofi, GSK, and Celgene, to develop new drug candidates using their AI platform.
Exscientia.ai has reported several successful milestones, including the development of the first AI-designed drug to enter clinical trials in 2020. The company has also received several awards and accolades for its innovative approach to drug discovery, including being named one of the world''s top 100 AI companies by CB Insights.
According to Zoominfo and based on annual reports, currently employs 285 people in UK (Oxford), Japan and USA. REvenues 30-40m USD per annum. Still heavily investing in R&amp;D at 60m USD per annum, so not yet profitable, but significant cash reserves.
