CIO, Eileen Jennings-Brown,  John knows several second connections of hers, looks like she is a keen networker, was in the top 50 women in tech recently. Knows John contacts at CITF and is linked to former Savannah head hunter Cathy Holley who now runs a coaching business. Very focussed on women in technology and promoting their causes. Has links with Scottish industry, is based in Dundee (same location as Mukesh of Platinum). Recently attended women in tech event there.

Richard Cox - VP Product and engineering - John has reached out to connect with him after being introduced by CHris Martin. HE is ex Imperial College alumni - did an MSC Chemistry there 1991 - 1995 (any overlap with Andy?). Also based in Dundee. Doesnt post a huge amount of linkedin, seems to have stopped a couple of years back. On his profile he talks about the desire to focus on DETAIL in execution in engineering and the desire to then spend 10% of time learning new skills.

Garry Pairaudeau - CTO - think he probably is head of architecture and strategy, but might actually be business side scientist CTO, not sure form profile. 25 year career at Astra Zeneca where he was senior in R&amp;D IT.  Looks like he has v strong science background, recenetly presented online on the scientific progress in their business together with their Chief Scientific Officer

John Overington - https://www.linkedin.com/in/joverington/ - data discovery scientist based in Houston, a lot of mutual connections with JH, including a connect to Rad at Eagle Genomics. Worth exploring whether Rad knows him well but he has a lot of connections so it might be one of those where they dont know each other well, but we should check...

Sujit Tandadpalliwar - https://www.linkedin.com/in/sujit-tangadpalliwar-mba-ph-d-3015a53a/ - Data scientist - connected to Atima Bhatnagar, johns ex GSK friend from Benevolent AI, John to check whether its a useful connection.


GT Approach
Initial meetings and introductions via CHris Martin with RIchard Cox, lets major on our credentials based on the track record we built with Platinum and what we built there. Send in advance our marketing deck summarising the key engineers we have placed in other clients.
In the first conversation, listen well, understand what their challenges are, try and understand current hiring patterns and needs. Play on Johns Life Science credentials, that enables us to have an understanding of critical and challenging scientific issues and ability to get the right engineers that really perform  this space.  In the discussion play back the fact that we understand his emphasis on DETAIL EXECUTION, use some examples where we know that  we did this well, Platinum and Eagle are the key examples.
Other connections - JH suspects that the CIO Eileen is the critical influencer and decision maker above Richard, aim to get connected to her in some way. The other links we have may be useful, but prioritise Chris, Richard and Eileen
Marketing - think about angles where we have relevance and which might get read by their key execs like Eileen, for example, can we promote an article about women in science, maybe linked to Eagle or to one of our other clients, lets figure out how to get the right stories and see if they get clicked through



