  (-453943531716::bigint, 453943531716::bigint, 'Hi Jacqui & Paul

It was great to talk openly this afternoon and here is a summary of my thoughts.

As per the analogy with the house around foundational issues, extensions and redecoration - the key gaps I think you need to close to enable solid delivery with the maximum efficiency are outlined below, together with the solution and recommended approach.

Please don''t share this as it is due to sensitive comments below. These comments should be removed before sharing with the team.

Let me know what you think, Andrew





THE GAPS

Foundations
This breakdowns into two areas: Tech & Process
• Tech - Areas of code to be addressed to optimise the code and minimise the time/costs for future changes, reduce maintenance effort and bugs.
• Insight Layer - Enable better more flexible reporting and facilitate easier testing 
• Gateway / Assembly - To ease setup and install of the gateways and reduce the spec of boxes required 
• The Rest - From talking to the team the rest is pretty solid but could do with tidying up when it next needs to be touched for new features

• Process - There are number of areas that should be addressed to improve the efficiency of delivery and the quality of your solution
Architecture - You need a handful of diagrams to outline the current architecture and target architecture so everyone is aligned with the vision and understands how your product works from a technical perspective. This reduces your dependance on one or two people that understand how things work and helps development and testing.Automated Testing Coverage - Improve your coverage of automated tests to enable earlier and quicker testing by developers and reduce the number of bugs / delivery timelines.Requirements / Non-functional Requirements - An outline of the product and how it works from a users perspective to aid onboarding, testing and developmentNon-functional testing - Ensure your non-functional testing is up to date. I don''t believe your security testing has been done since Jan 2024 and should be done regularly with the current levels of change and I don''t know if you have done Business Continuity / Disaster Recovery plans or testing.Agile Improvements - More accurately load sprints and track burn down rates to improve estimates going forwards. Also increase the quality of and attendance of demosCommunications - Comms from the tech team to the rest of the business need to be lifted up a level providing concise summaries with clear updates on progressClient Engagement - Consider doing pilots with one or more clients - listen to what they need and deliver on the basis that they will be happy to do PR upon successful completion / buy X UnitsExtensions
New features as per the Roadmap in the GT deck and Andre''s doc. Andre''s estimates look good and the context / detail is helpful. I think it needs a clearer timeline, confirmation from the business with respect to the changes vs the GT deck - eg: B2C comes before ICS but otherwise content is good.

Redecoration
Everything from the install to the websites, apps and reports could be more usable and the look & feel can be improved to engage clients.

THE SOLUTIONS

Foundations
Tech & Architecture - Get an Architect to review architecture and code. This could be positioned to support Tim and document his vision for his and everyone''s benefit. This will also give direction on whether we are doing the right thing in persisting with the existing code base.Test Coverage - Two automation testers brought in to increase coverage to an acceptable level in a single burst while the rest of the team focus on new featuresReq / NFRs - Get Andre document (if it is not already done in a wiki that I haven''t seen)NFRs - Get Ben / Tim to book / execute pen / BC/DR testing when it is appropriate.Overall / Agile Improvements / Communications - Get CTO / Andrew in part-time to get right processes and comms in place and oversee timely deliveryClient Engagement - Get Andre / Steve to select ASC clients with needs that closely match our roadmap for input to development and a case study. BTW if they are not aligned to our roadmap something may not be right with our roadmap.Extension
Bring in addition resources to deliver the outlined roadmap within the timelines and determine the capabilities of the current team

Redecoration
Improve UX / UI



THE RECOMMENDED APPROACH

