  (-173518525627::bigint, 173518525627::bigint, 'As promised I am connecting you Jake Arnold-Forster CEO and co-founder of Carradale Futures which I chair. The business owns and operates a platform that helps client organisations to standardise, improve and audit their standard operating procedures (SOPs).  Carradale’s platform enables these organisations to rapidly create a detailed digital blueprint of their processes - a foundational step to effective automation. Onboarding is quick and easy with AI assisted transformation of existing governance and process documentation.

  

You can see a brief demo video re how it is used here https://vimeo.com/user160819127/sophia-governance.

 

The business started in the healthcare sector and has hospital and mental health trust clients in the UK, Australia & Barbados for whom Carradale’s platform and consultancy team have been helping drive significant improvements in productivity, cost reduction and quality assurance/safety across thousands of operational processes involving 30,000+ employee users. Carradale raised expansion funds from Bayes Entrepreneurship Fund in 2024, which is part of Bayes Business School & City University in London, and has since started to expand into other sectors such as local government, higher education, pharmacy, professional services, hospitality and agriculture.

 

Clients include NHS Essex Partnership University Trust, NHS West London Trust, Ashford and St Peters Hospital, NHS Central London Community Healthcare, Barwon Health (regional health provider in Australia), Greenlight Pharmacies, NHS East Cheshire Trust, QE Hospital Barbados, SoilLess Farms (Nigeria), Elivated Edge (hotel management group).

 

Background for Jake – John Harris is CTO of GT Life Sciences which help life science companies manage their digital development and data services. GT clients include Boots, Eagle Genomics and Mundi Pharma. Attached are a couple of explanatory docs on the business.', 'JH', '2025-04-08 06:04'),
